{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic","id":1520086,"title":"I figured out Chi Magic!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-08T01:17:02-07:00","id":1520086,"title":"I figured out Chi Magic!","content":"When HDYDT came out, one of its biggest criticisms was Sphere bloat. This was the idea that the book demanded so many effects required far more spheres and at higher rank than was needed previously.<br /> <br /> one of the more noteworthy forms of this was elements in the book that implied one\u2019s paradigm dictated when you needed extra spheres to do otherwise similar effects, this was what was cited for the Shaman\u2019s \u2018a bit of spirit\u2019 \u2018psychics\u2019 need of Mind, and the ever infamous requirement of Prime 2 for daring to believe in Chi.<br /> <br /> Since then, I have reinterpreted these supposed rulings and found a way for them to make sense. For Shaman, the idea was without spirit, they were directing the spirits of, for example, fire, without direct communication, but Spirit enabled them that line of communication, meaning the flame spirit could take over if agreeable. For psychics, Mind allowed their effect to be more than a one and done. Forces 2 lets you move fire about in a single instant effecg, Mind along with this let you instead have an duration effect where you could telekinetically make fire move as you please. Without mind, the psychic could achieve the same ends, but they would need to roll arete for each and every movement of the flame.<br /> <br /> for a while, I was stumped by how to make sense of Chi magic. Their insistence to add Prime 2 to everything in order to \u201crearrange your energies\u201d didn\u2019t give much to see what Prime 2 actually did for the effect. Especially as the only mechanical difference between the effect with Prime 2 and without was now you had to spend quintessence just to do it. <br /> <br /> But now I have an answer. What Chi effects do is turn quintessence itself in to a single use trinket.<br /> <br /> to explain, a trinket is a wonder which has a \u2018locked\u2019 effect within it, usually some warp of reality like invisibility, reduced gravity, good luck, etc.<br /> <br /> what Chi techniques do is \u2018lock\u2019 an effect within your pool of quintessence, such that they manifest upon the expenditure of said quintessence. This enchantment on your quintessence pool remains for the duration of the effect<br /> <br /> lets use Chi Flight as an example. Life 2/Forces 2/Prime 2<br /> <br /> the effect allows you to do some of the wu shu style jumps to get to impossible hights and breadths.<br /> <br /> <br /> the Forces 2 allows you to suspend gravity for flight while Life 2 lets you modulate your weight in lock step, letting you jump about light as a feather, as is seen in many wu shu films where the fighters are jumping from tree branch to tree branch. Forces alone lets you make the jump, and if you affect the whole area, help with the landing, and Life 2 alone can make you weigh less allowing for easier jumps and landings in a way that only impacts you, though the two together allow you to jump and land with the grace the films portray without changing gravity for everyone in the area.<br /> <br /> however, you would need to cast this at the point of use. What I propose Prime 2 adds to the effect is it lets you enchant your own pool of quintessence with these effects, allowing you to cast the effect ahead of time, hold it for the duration, and then let it go upon the expenditure of the enchanted quintessence point.<br /> <br /> this would allow you to do this chi flight effect multiple times during the scene with only a single cast just by spending the point of quintessence.<br /> <br /> this can be applied to Chi Healing as well, essentially making quintessence behave like a vampire\u2019s bloodpool for the purposes of healing for the duration of the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T05:15:57-07:00","id":1520096,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting thought, but does this imply that the enchanted point of quintessence is now locked up and not usable for anything else? Mechanically is this much different from an effect hung with Time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T06:17:24-07:00","id":1520099,"title":"","content":"My first thought is that no single point of quintessence from your pool is now \u2018locked up\u2019 by the effect. This is because I see quintessence as a fairly fluid energy. As long as it comes from within, it is a part of your energy that the effect draws from.<br /> <br /> This means if you use quintessence for other purposes, you simply have less of this energy to draw from for you active chi effect, but you also don\u2019t partition away quintessence for specific uses. So you could have a few chi effects running in duration and only trigger one of them a few times by spending quint as and when desire.<br /> <br /> I imagine this technique differs from Time 4 style suspended effects in the following key ways<br /> <br /> 1. Time 4 triggers are inflexible once cast. Chi effects don\u2019t have to be set off once cast, they can simply be on going effects you have access to but choose not to use, or choose to use several times until your exhaust your quintessence.<br /> <br /> 2. Time 4 effects don\u2019t need you there to be set off, Chi effects are still centred on you and your interactions. It is in this way much more similar to operating a Wonder than it is delaying an effect.<br /> <br /> 3. Time 4 effects don\u2019t require active concentration to maintain, but arguably Chi effects should. This gets a bit subjective as people can say technically any effect that has duration does not contribute to multiple effects limit, but I would argue that effects that require active concentration to be maintained are not included in this. With that interpretation in mind, concentrating your chi for an extended period like this takes your attention, and as such I would suggest it will contribute to that climbing difficulty.<br /> <br /> 4. Time 4 effects will work regardless of your quintessence pool. Chi effects are entirely dependent on the quality of your quintessence. This means resonance will be a heavy factor. If your quintessence source matches your own, either because it comes from your personal pool, your life pool via haarts blood, or from a soulgem, then all should be well. If it comes from a node, periapt, tass, the air, or another person, then that resonance will have an impact on how the effect itself manifests, this will be very much up to the ST how that plays out.<br /> <br /> Regarding paradox. There are two ways to play it.<br /> <br /> one way is to use Wonder rules, where paradox may be accrued upon using the wonder (spending the quint). Whether it is coincidental or vulgar depends on how it looks at the point of expenditure. And beyond the initial cast, would not risk botches.<br /> <br /> second way is to use Time 4 casting rules. If there is a possibility for the effect to be vulgar once set off, then it is a vulgar effect, even if it never actually gets set off. If you want to cast it as a coincidental effect, then you simply won\u2019t be able to use quint for that effect to do vulgar things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T07:42:48-07:00","id":1520109,"title":"","content":"10 for the mental gymnastics. Truly on Olympic level.<br /> <br /> But seriously, no. Fly requires Forces alone, Life is doing nothing there (you don't have to mess with your weight to fly). Forces 2 allows you to fly like superman. You don't need anything else to land.<br /> Telekinesis requires concentration (iirc) but I'm not sure you need an Arete roll per turn, this seems harsh.<br /> <br /> Your quintessence wheel isn't a thing in game. It isn't a pattern that you can lock an effect nor make a wonder from it. Also, blackwell was on point when he asked if that wouldn't make Prime 2 quite similar to Time 4 hanging spell.<br /> <br /> Having said that, if the Chi mahe doesn't want to make trinkets or change his weight or any of that. What if he just want to manipulate garavity to fly through chi? How would that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T08:43:05-07:00","id":1520112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fly requires Forces alone, Life is doing nothing there (you don't have to mess with your weight to fly). Forces 2 allows you to fly like superman. You don't need anything else to land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flight can be achieved in a variety of ways. By Forces it can be done by shifting gravity, introducing a gust of wind, or changing your momentum. Life can achieve a similar effect by reducing your body\u2019s weight significantly or by enhancing your strength such that your jump would achieve a similar end.<br /> <br /> as with every effect, the specifics of what your effect does will introduce caveats in how it enacts. Changing gravity in an area will affect everything, not just yourself. While changing your momentum will get you going in a direction, but you\u2019ll need another cast to shift it or slow it if you don\u2019t build the change in speed into the effect from the outset.<br /> <br /> Using the two methods, in this case Forces for gravity and Life for weight, allow both these effects to work in tandem with one another, providing the benefits that both allow. They are additive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Telekinesis requires concentration (iirc) but I'm not sure you need an Arete roll per turn, this seems harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>telekenisis can be achieved a number of different ways. One way is by correspondence with matter to hold objects from a distance and move them as though they were in your hand, even if they are on the other side of the rolm<br /> <br /> Another is via Forces by either changing gravity around the object or changing the object\u2019s momentum. The first may make the object float if disturbed whole the other makes the object move in a direction. You can combine these effects by giving a patch of low gravity momentum and have the object caught within it, but to change the momentum, it\u2019s speed or direction, would require another cast to pull off, at least going RAW.<br /> <br /> what Mind 3 Forces 3, you can transmute your thoughts in to forces patterns, such as in to momentum. With this effect active, you can focus on your target and change the momentum of it as you think on it. This would not be tied to the object, but to any object you focus on, and such a telekinetic power would last the length of duration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Your quintessence wheel isn't a thing in game. It isn't a pattern that you can lock an effect nor make a wonder from it. Also, blackwell was on point when he asked if that wouldn't make Prime 2 quite similar to Time 4 hanging spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can target quintessence with Prime to move it about, solidify it, and change its properties, like its resonance, in many ways it behaves like an ephemeral pattern, not unlike spirit.<br /> <br /> regarding Time 4, I believe I already addressed these concerns in the post just above yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Having said that, if the Chi mahe doesn't want to make trinkets or change his weight or any of that. What if he just want to manipulate garavity to fly through chi? How would that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>like a Forces effect. And how it would work would depend on which Forces effect they used.<br /> <br /> if you manipulate gravity in an area, then everyone in the patch of changed gravity will be affected. You could instead have it work as a single burst localised specifically around you to push you for the jump, in which case they would need to cast the effect ever time they wanted to jump like that. You could instead put duration in to the gravity effect, but that would keep it mapped to the space you effect by default, so if you move away from that patch of gravity, the effect stays there unless locked to something you carry with you, or to your pattern via Life 3<br /> <br /> Again, the other spheres offer additives to this effect, forces lets the movement change, Life lowers diff to jump and land, and Prime enables one to set it off upon expenditure of quintessence later on, making it a more flexible application.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T08:45:40-07:00","id":1520113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon