ect, forces lets the movement change, Life lowers diff to jump and land, and Prime enables one to set it off upon expenditure of quintessence later on, making it a more flexible application.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T09:41:54-07:00","id":1520121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fly requires Forces alone, Life is doing nothing there (you don't have to mess with your weight to fly). Forces 2 allows you to fly like superman. You don't need anything else to land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flight can be achieved in a variety of ways. By Forces it can be done by shifting gravity, introducing a gust of wind, or changing your momentum. Life can achieve a similar effect by reducing your body\u2019s weight significantly or by enhancing your strength such that your jump would achieve a similar end.<br /> <br /> as with every effect, the specifics of what your effect does will introduce caveats in how it enacts. Changing gravity in an area will affect everything, not just yourself. While changing your momentum will get you going in a direction, but you\u2019ll need another cast to shift it or slow it if you don\u2019t build the change in speed into the effect from the outset.<br /> <br /> Using the two methods, in this case Forces for gravity and Life for weight, allow both these effects to work in tandem with one another, providing the benefits that both allow. They are additive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Telekinesis requires concentration (iirc) but I'm not sure you need an Arete roll per turn, this seems harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>telekenisis can be achieved a number of different ways. One way is by correspondence with matter to hold objects from a distance and move them as though they were in your hand, even if they are on the other side of the rolm<br /> <br /> Another is via Forces by either changing gravity around the object or changing the object\u2019s momentum. The first may make the object float if disturbed whole the other makes the object move in a direction. You can combine these effects by giving a patch of low gravity momentum and have the object caught within it, but to change the momentum, it\u2019s speed or direction, would require another cast to pull off, at least going RAW.<br /> <br /> what Mind 3 Forces 3, you can transmute your thoughts in to forces patterns, such as in to momentum. With this effect active, you can focus on your target and change the momentum of it as you think on it. This would not be tied to the object, but to any object you focus on, and such a telekinetic power would last the length of duration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Your quintessence wheel isn't a thing in game. It isn't a pattern that you can lock an effect nor make a wonder from it. Also, blackwell was on point when he asked if that wouldn't make Prime 2 quite similar to Time 4 hanging spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can target quintessence with Prime to move it about, solidify it, and change its properties, like its resonance, in many ways it behaves like an ephemeral pattern, not unlike spirit.<br /> <br /> regarding Time 4, I believe I already addressed these concerns in the post just above yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Having said that, if the Chi mahe doesn't want to make trinkets or change his weight or any of that. What if he just want to manipulate garavity to fly through chi? How would that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>like a Forces effect. And how it would work would depend on which Forces effect they used.<br /> <br /> if you manipulate gravity in an area, then everyone in the patch of changed gravity will be affected. You could instead have it work as a single burst localised specifically around you to push you for the jump, in which case they would need to cast the effect ever time they wanted to jump like that. You could instead put duration in to the gravity effect, but that would keep it mapped to the space you effect by default, so if you move away from that patch of gravity, the effect stays there unless locked to something you carry with you, or to your pattern via Life 3<br /> <br /> Again, the other spheres offer additives to this effect, forces lets the movement change, Life lowers diff to jump and land, and Prime enables one to set it off upon expenditure of quintessence later on, making it a more flexible application.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"