-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Your quintessence wheel isn't a thing in game. It isn't a pattern that you can lock an effect nor make a wonder from it. Also, blackwell was on point when he asked if that wouldn't make Prime 2 quite similar to Time 4 hanging spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can target quintessence with Prime to move it about, solidify it, and change its properties, like its resonance, in many ways it behaves like an ephemeral pattern, not unlike spirit.<br /> <br /> regarding Time 4, I believe I already addressed these concerns in the post just above yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520109#post1520109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Having said that, if the Chi mahe doesn't want to make trinkets or change his weight or any of that. What if he just want to manipulate garavity to fly through chi? How would that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>like a Forces effect. And how it would work would depend on which Forces effect they used.<br /> <br /> if you manipulate gravity in an area, then everyone in the patch of changed gravity will be affected. You could instead have it work as a single burst localised specifically around you to push you for the jump, in which case they would need to cast the effect ever time they wanted to jump like that. You could instead put duration in to the gravity effect, but that would keep it mapped to the space you effect by default, so if you move away from that patch of gravity, the effect stays there unless locked to something you carry with you, or to your pattern via Life 3<br /> <br /> Again, the other spheres offer additives to this effect, forces lets the movement change, Life lowers diff to jump and land, and Prime enables one to set it off upon expenditure of quintessence later on, making it a more flexible application.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T10:01:14-07:00","id":1520131,"title":"","content":"Hmm, for me different 'flavors' of Quintessence isn't such a strange thought, and Prime 2 to convert QE into another type makes sense. I mean, Chi is literally one of the Power Fuel stats in another splat. Gnosis, Sekhem, Chi, Mana (pre-S20) and even Vitae are <i>functionally </i>the same stuff, but the flavor matters in what kind of powers they can fuel. If Chi is needed to make you monk out, you'll have to convert the QE into that flavor first. S20 also requires the Quintessence Manipulation Path now if you want to make use of the Chi merits.<br /> <br /> I think of it as different types of catalysts you would need to make different types of chemical reactions go. Let's take one of the possible cross-splats as example, a Kinfolk Mage. You would still have your separate Gnosis and Quintessence pools, and I would say Prime 2 is fair to convert one into the other. So for Chi Magick, maybe opening a separate Chi pool would be the easiest solution. That way instead of locking an effect in, you're locking in how much of your QE is dedicated to fueling it. Sorcerer Revised did that with a Background that allowed you to store up to 5 dots worth of Mana in your pattern, I see no reason why the same couldn't be done with Chi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T10:04:18-07:00","id":1520133,"title":"","content":"I like the principle of what Saikou is suggesting; but I'm not so fond of the implementation. Here's my take on Chi Magick:<br /> <br /> Chi Magick is a way to imbue mundane Abilities with Magickal Effects. Chi Flight isn't Flight; it tweaks reality in ways that allows Athletics to do something that it normally couldn't: run up walls, or along tree-tops, or across the surface of a pond; that sort of thing. The brute force approach to this would be to use Forces \u2022\u2022 to almost-but-not-quite-fly; but Chi Magick uses a subtler approach by imbuing the ability to move along surfaces that would normally not support him into his Athletics. Likewise, Chi Healing imbues Medicine with supernatural potency, letting it go beyond the normal bounds of what Medicine can normally accomplish. The War-Power Chi Shout imbues Intimidation with a supernatural menace. And so on.<br /> <br /> The game system for this is rather straightforward: by incorporating Prime \u2022\u2022 into the Effect and spending a point of Quintessence per use, the mage gets to add a suitable Ability to the dice pool for the Effect: for example, you don't roll Arete; you roll Arete+Athletics.<br /> <br /> It's not used all the time because it's <i>expensive</i>; Quintessence is something of a limited resource. But it has the potential to make your dice pool <i>much</i> larger, and thus pull off more potent Feats of Magick without having to resort to rituals.<br /> <br /> This is in keeping with some of the reinterpretations of Prime that started with <i>Convention Book: Syndicate</i>, where Prime takes on a more abstract sense than \u201cmerely\u201d being a mystical energy. If you can \u201cdraw power\u201d from human activities, then you should be able to <i>imbue</i> human activities with power.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell: this isn't \u201cAbilities Enhancing Magick\u201d or \u201cMagick Enhancing Abilities\u201d; it's \u201cMagickal Abilities\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-08-2023, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T05:58:27-07:00","id":1520189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520099#post1520099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Time 4 effects don\u2019t require active concentration to maintain, but arguably Chi effects should. This gets a bit subjective as people can say technically any effect that has duration does not contribute to multiple effects limit, but I would argue that effects that require active concentration to be maintained are not included in this. With that interpretation in mind, concentrating your chi for an extended period like this takes your attention, and as such I would suggest it will contribute to that climbing difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way the effect shouldn't require quintessence per raw. Yes, effects that require concentration count for the limit of 2 effects per +1 diff. The ones that do not require concentration do not count for that limit. No option requires quint.<br /> <br /> Now, I can see a house rule that makes you spend quint when using your internal energy as fuel. But then, only effects that creates a pattern from nothing. So, you cold reate fire with Prime+Forces, or Mind+Forces (to transform mental energy into fire) or just Forces+ quint (meaning that you spend your own energy to fuel). But fly and healing do not require fuel. Any effect that doesn't require Prime shouldn't require quint when you don't have Prime. <br /> <br /> I know there are several way to do effects, but adding Life to fly shoulnd't be a <b>requirement</b> (as it is in hdydt). If the player wants to make the effect in a way that his body weight changes, then ok, add Life. Note that <b>the spheres involved depend on what the effect does and not what instruments are being used.</b>. And that's my issue with the whole hi thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T07:25:36-07:00","id":1520194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520189#post1520189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Either way the effect shouldn't require quintessence per raw. Yes, effects that require concentration count for the limit of 2 effects per +1 diff. The ones that do not require concentration do not count for that limit. No option requires quint.<br /> <br /> Now, I can see a house rule that makes you spend quint when using your internal energy as fuel. But then, only effects that creates a pattern from nothing. So, you cold reate fire with Prime+Forces, or Mind+Forces (to transform mental energy into fire) or just Forces+ quint (meaning that you spend your own energy to fuel). But fly and healing do not require fuel. Any effect that doesn't require Prime shouldn't require quint when you don't have Prime.<br /> <br /> I know there are several way to do effects, but adding Life to fly shoulnd't be a <b>requirement</b> (as it is in hdydt). If the player wants to make the effect in a way that his body weight changes, then ok, add Life. Note that <b>the spheres involved depend on what the effect does and not what instruments are being used.</b>. And that's my issue with the whole hi thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the impression that you\u2019re arguing more against the language of the book than with me.<br /> <br /> as far as I\u2019m concerned, nothing I am suggesting is the case of \u201cdifferent instruments require different spheres\u201d<br /> <br /> all I\u2019m saying is, if you want to alter gravity, use forces, if you want to alter gravity and your weight, use Forces and Life, if you want to alter gravity and your weight in short bursts at key moments during a scene without needing to roll arete every time you wish to do the effect, use Prime so you can have the effect \u2018activatable\u2019 for the scene upon the expenditure of quint.<br /> <br /> the full effect as I describe it is fir the duration of the effect, you can gain the bonus to your jumps for any one roll upon the expenditure of quint, this can be done as many times as you have quint to spare without a second arete roll required.<br /> <br /> similarly, the proposal with chi healing would be that, for the duration of the effect, you can spend quint to heal in the same way a vampire exchanges blood or a wraith exchanges pathos to heal.<br /> <br /> the Life alone version would need an arete roll at the point of wanting to heal, and each time you wish to heal, a new arete roll would be required. The Chi version casts the effect ahead of the scene, and for the duration of the scene, you may exchange quint for health whenever you wish as many times as you like, so long as you have enough quint, no further arete rolls needed<br /> <br /> <br /> and note, I only call it \u201cthe Chi version\u201d, in the same way a shaman can use Forces to communicate with the spirits of elements indirectly, a Chi mage can concentrate on their Chi with just Life to heal, it\u2019s just that of the Shaman also used spirit, they would have more options via direct spirit communications, as the Chi mage would have more options due to active focus on the personal quintessence part of their Chi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T09:07:40-07:00","id":1520209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520194#post1520194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the impression that you\u2019re arguing more against the language of the book than with me.<br /> <br /> as far as I\u2019m concerned, nothing I am suggesting is the case of \u201cdifferent instruments require different spheres\u201d<br /> <br /> all I\u2019m saying is, if you want to alter gravity, use forces, if you want to alter gravity and your weight, use Forces and Life, if you want to alter gravity and your weight in short bursts at key moments during a scene without needing to roll arete every time you wish to do the effect, use Prime so you can have the effect \u2018activatable\u2019 for the scene upon the expenditure of quint.<br /> <br /> the full effect as I describe it is fir the duration of the effect, you can gain the bonus to your jumps for any one roll upon the expenditure of quint, this can be done as many times as you have quint to spare without a second arete roll required.<br /> <br /> similarly, the proposal with chi healing would be that, for the duration of the effect, you can spend quint to heal in the same way a vampire exchanges blood or a wraith exchanges pathos to heal.<br /> <br /> the Life alone version would need an arete roll at the point of wanting to heal, and each time you wish to heal, a new arete roll would be required. The Chi version casts the effect ahead of the scene, and for the duration of the scene, you may exchange quint for health whenever you wish as many times as you like, so long as you have enough quint, no further arete rolls needed<br /> <br /> <br /> and note, I only call it \u201cthe Chi version\u201d, in the same way a shaman can use Forces to communicate with the spirits of elements indirectly, a Chi mage can concentrate on their Chi with just Life to heal, it\u2019s just that of the Shaman also used spirit, they would have more options via direct spirit communications, as the Chi mage would have more options due to active focus on the personal quintessence part of their Chi</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I had the impression that you was trying to explain what the Chi part of hdydt was intended to work by the authors. I didn't tought you were creating a house-rule.<br /> <br /> As a house rule and an option for players that want to do that way, I think it's a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T15:43:01-07:00","id":1520239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520209#post1520209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. I had the impression that you was trying to explain what the Chi part of hdydt was intended to work by the authors. I didn't tought you were creating a house-rule.<br /> <br /> As a house rule and an option for players that want to do that way, I think it's a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what they were intending, but this is more of a interpretation attempt that closely follows the established logic of the spheres.<br /> <br /> there is a lot of good things in HDYDT, but there are also a lot of poorly communicated points and rather odd decisions. My aim is always to try and reinterpret the material that doesn\u2019t quite mesh through the filter of the established logic, and this is what I have come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T01:58:58-07:00","id":1520272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520133#post1520133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chi Magick is a way to imbue mundane Abilities with Magickal Effects. Chi Flight isn't Flight; it tweaks reality in ways that allows Athletics to do something that it normally couldn't: run up walls, or along tree-tops, or across the surface of a pond; that sort of thing. The brute force approach to this would be to use Forces \u2022\u2022 to almost-but-not-quite-fly; but Chi Magick uses a subtler approach by imbuing the ability to move along surfaces that would normally not support him into his Athletics. Likewise, Chi Healing imbues Medicine with supernatural potency, letting it go beyond the normal bounds of what Medicine can normally accomplish. The War-Power Chi Shout imbues Intimidation with a supernatural menace. And so on.<br /> <br /> The game system for this is rather straightforward: by incorporating Prime \u2022\u2022 into the Effect and spending a point of Quintessence per use, the mage gets to add a suitable Ability to the dice pool for the Effect: for example, you don't roll Arete; you roll Arete+Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like the idea of an effect that creates a new, entirely-impossible enhancement, that game system for it doesn\u2019t look like it fits, to me.<br /> <br /> There is already a mechanism for spending Quintessence to improve an effect: -1 difficulty to the Arete roll per Quintessence. While it could be in keeping with general principles to allow the addition of a Sphere to allow the use of more advantageous mechanics, adding a whole new ability to the Arete roll will often double the casting dice pool. It seems like an outsized boost for Prime 2, and not really very representative of the effect. How does those extra dice rolled translate into the new application of an ability?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T03:06:36-07:00","id":1520276,"title":"","content":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bI had originally considered posing it as a variant of Violence as a Focus: make a Magick roll to temporarily imbue your Ability with a Magickal use, then (in the same turn) make an Ability roll to use it. <br /> <br /> I rejected this idea as being too clunky, and not something that you'd need Prime to do: Violence as a Focus doesn't require Prime. But that's what I was using as the baseline to decide whether my mechanism was overpowered. <br /> <br /> While I described what I finally decided on as adding Ability dice to the Arete pool, it would be equally fair to describe it as using Arete as the Attribute in a traditional Attribute+Ability pool; and that is, in fact, my preferred way of looking at it: instead of making an Arete roll followed by an Attribute+Ability roll, the inclusion of Prime \u2022\u2022 lets you combine them into a single dice pool. Looking at it that way, you're not really getting more dice for the Magickal use of the Ability than you'd get for a mundane use of the Ability; you'd just be changing the Attribute from a mundane one to the Magickal one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T07:47:34-07:00","id":1520297,"title":"","content":"Something like Utility Attainments from Awakening for Ascension? Sounds good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T18:00:52-07:00","id":1520347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520276#post1520276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> While I described what I finally decided on as adding Ability dice to the Arete pool, it would be equally fair to describe it as using Arete as the Attribute in a traditional Attribute+Ability pool; and that is, in fact, my preferred way of looking at it: instead of making an Arete roll followed by an Attribute+Ability roll, the inclusion of Prime \u2022\u2022 lets you combine them into a single dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Arete+Ability is being used in place of a regular Attribute+Ability roll, that\u2019s fairly reasonable. But if that pool is being rolled for casting the effect, that\u2019s a whole lot of extra potential successes. Since the results on casting rolls are calibrated for Arete alone, that\u2019s going to add up real fast for typical PC power levels, especially starting characters with their hard limit of 3 on Arete.<br /> <br /> And if you are applying that as a substitute for the Attribute+Ability roll, your casting roll seems to have disappeared completely. Which means no chance of outright failure, or a Paradox-inducing botch. Even if you consider no successes to be a failure of the effect, and a botch to incur Paradox, on the Arete+Ability roll, the probabilities of those occurring go way down.<br /> <br /> Finally, if Arete+Ability is being read as having the effects of Atttribute+Ability (rather than applying successes to achieving a magickal feat) I\u2019m not sure how to translate that into an otherwise-impossible supernatural feat. More successes on an Athletics roll allow running a bit faster. How many successes instead turn into running across the surface of water?<br /> <br /> You might have answers to these concerns. I\u2019m just not seeing them in your description so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520276#post1520276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bLooking at it that way, you're not really getting more dice for the Magickal use of the Ability than you'd get for a mundane use of the Ability; you'd just be changing the Attribute from a mundane one to the Magickal one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, an experienced character will often be getting more dice even so, due to Arete being on a 1-10 scale instead of a 1-5 scale. But for those more experienced characters, that may be desirable, depending on how the results of the roll are applied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T04:29:35-07:00","id":1520373,"title":"","content":"I would use a variation of the Dividing Successes optional rule on M20 p.538: roll the dice as usual, then split the successes between the enabling Feat and the use of the Ability. If you're that worried about the mismatch in pool sizes, you can insist that no more than half of the successes can go to the enabling Magick, and the rest must go to the Ability roll.<br /> <br /> It's largely a moot point, though, because the enabling Effect is almost always accomplished with a single success: M537 says that \u201c<i>Personal Effects</i> that make minor changes in your character's own reality require only one success. These include sensory perception enhancements, divinations, self-healing, temporary trait boosts, minor cosmetic changes (hair color, skin color, height, etc ) and the like. Extreme or long-lasting alterations \u2014 radical shape changes, multiple selves, transformations into elemental forces, and so forth \u2014 require three successes or more.\u201d <br /> <br /> \u2022 The Chi-Fire Punch is a trivial example of this: you enchant yourself so that your next strike does aggravated damage.<br /> \u2022 Chi Flight is this, too: instead of actually <i>flying</i>, you run along surfaces that normally wouldn't support you; or you move through the air as if you were in low gravity instead of as if it was zero gravity. As well, the bulk of what Chi Flight does (in this view of things) is accomplished by your Athletics, not your Magick per se: you'd be rolling the likes of Chase, Climbing, or Jumping (M20 p.403); all that the Magick does is to alter how you interact with your environment, allowing you to move as if there were wires supporting your weight and pulling you around. <br /> \u2022 Chi-Healing can be thought of this as well: conceptually, it's like being able to use the \u201cPatch 'Em Up\u201d optional rule on M20 p.409 without the downsides such as needing a lengthy recuperation afterward: the removal of the downsides is \u201call\u201d that the Magick does. One, <i>maybe</i> two successes to the Effect; the rest to the Medicine task. <br /> \u2022 The Spirit-Strike merely imbues the Chi user's next strike with the ability to treat appropriate insubstantial targets as if they were material; the actual attack mechanics do the rest. <br /> \u2022 The War Power Chi Shout explicitly references the Kiaijutsu Iron Shout technique (M20 p.429), which doesn't require the Magickal casting rules to use; the Life 3/Mind 2/Prime 2 Effect described on HDYDT pp.65\u201366 basically serve as an alternate prerequisite for the technique, letting the Chi Magician pull it off without needing to invest dots into Do. In this case, and indeed any other Special Do Techniques that the Storyteller decides should be accessible using Chi Magick instead of actually studying Do, I'd go with Attribute+Arete rolls instead of Arete+Ability rolls: substitute Arete for Do. <br /> <br /> The only Chi Effects from HDYDT that I'd require multiple successes be dedicated to the empowerment part would be the Chi-Field Push (unless you reinterpret that as a variation of the Hurricane Throw Do technique, M20 pp.428\u2013429), the Chi-Vampire Strike, and Elemental Fury Chi; and even there, you're still using the Martial Arts Ability to do the actual attack: all that the empowering Effect of Chi-Vampire Strike does is to change damage inflicted into Quintessence drained; and Elemental Fury Chi, arguably the only one of these that might require more than two successes going into the Magick, adds appropriate elemental damage to the mundane damage of your regular Martial Arts strike. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> Bottom line, you're rarely going to be putting more than one or two successes into the empowering Effect; the rest goes straight into performing the Ability's task. So there's a slight drain on the \u201cmundane\u201d effectiveness of the task being performed; but that's easily compensated for by the Magickal benefits added to it. Which is why a Quintessence cost is appropriate in most cases: otherwise, it might be a bit <i>too</i> good of a deal. <br /> <br /> Chi Magick mostly isn't about performing Mighty Feats with Magick; it's about using a touch of Magick (mostly Simple Feats, occasionally Standard Feats) to leverage what your Abilities can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T06:36:31-07:00","id":1520383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520373#post1520373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would use a variation of the Dividing Successes optional rule on M20 p.538: roll the dice as usual, then split the successes between the enabling Feat and the use of the Ability. If you're that worried about the mismatch in pool sizes, you can insist that no more than half of the successes can go to the enabling Magick, and the rest must go to the Ability roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Maybe. The maths is still tricky, but it might be alright.<br /> <br /> It does occur to me that issues with the increased size of the pool and its effect on outright failure and botching might be dealt with by keeping the Arete roll separate, and then roll just Ability and add any successes left over from achieving the necessary effect. The usual effect of Magick Enhancing\u2026 is to add a die per success on the Arete roll to the roll you want to enhance, so it\u2019s potentially still better than that depending on the number of successes required for the effect vs the size of the Arete pool. Actually, the really big benefit of this is allowing it all to be done in the same round without penalty from the multiple actions rules. Taking that into account, it\u2019s a very good enhancement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520373#post1520373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's largely a moot point, though, because the enabling Effect is almost always accomplished with a single success: M537 says that \u201c<i>Personal Effects</i> that make minor changes in your character's own reality require only one success. These include sensory perception enhancements, divinations, self-healing, temporary trait boosts, minor cosmetic changes (hair color, skin color, height, etc ) and the like. Extreme or long-lasting alterations \u2014 radical shape changes, multiple selves, transformations into elemental forces, and so forth \u2014 require three successes or more.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing about that\u2026 The healing listed there is pretty specifically at odds with \u201cHealing yourself\u201d on the Magickal Feats chart on page 502 (and that is backed up by the Base Damage or Duration chart on page 504).<br /> <br /> And I think the real takeaway from that is that while an effect may occur with only one success, the magnitude of the effect will still vary with the number of successes. (I would favour resolving that discrepancy with healing specifically by realising that characters can suffer bodily harm at a level below what a single health level represents\u2026 so if you roll a single success on healing yourself, you can close over the fingerprick from when you tested your glucose levels earlier, but not the knife wound from where somebody stabbed you for a health level of damage.)<br /> <br /> Regardless, I\u2019m not convinced that supernatural flight is only a minor change in your reality, or equivalent to a change of hair or skin colour.<br /> <br /> And furthermore, it\u2019s not so much the book examples you want to apply this to that worry me. It\u2019s what other effects players will start to come up with once they do the maths on the mechanic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T07:11:07-07:00","id":1520384,"title":"","content":"Again, Chi Flight isn't Flight; you don't break free from the bonds of gravity and soar through the air. And <i>that's</i> a Standard Feat. Also, unlike Flight, Chi Flight doesn't propel you; you do your own running and jumping. So I can definitely see Chi Flight being a Simple Feat. <br /> <br /> As for self-healing, that's explicitly listed among the Simple Feats. My reference to \u201cPatch 'Em Up\u201d had to do with Chi Healing as it applies to others. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T08:14:24-07:00","id":1520387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520384#post1520384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, Chi Flight isn't Flight; you don't break free from the bonds of gravity and soar through the air. And <i>that's</i> a Standard Feat. Also, unlike Flight, Chi Flight doesn't propel you; you do your own running and jumping. So I can definitely see Chi Flight being a Simple Feat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve seen <i>Hero</i>, and <i>Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon</i>, explicitly given as inspiration for Chi Flight. The characters in question really do soar through the air, albeit for shorter distances than we see in <i>Superman</i>. I remain skeptical of calling it a simple feat.<br /> <br /> (If full-on flight is a standard feat, perhaps both are standard feats, and Chi Flight offers some advantage that Flight doesn\u2019t. For example, just running Chi Flight off of Athletics rather than Flying may well be all the advantage a mystical martial artist needs to give up accept the limitation of having to touch a treetop every 20 metres or so.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520384#post1520384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for self-healing, that's explicitly listed among the Simple Feats.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><b>And</b> it is explicitly listed among the Standard Feats. Seriously, check out page 502. (Unless the PDF has been errataed since the last time I downloaded it.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T09:05:46-07:00","id":1520390,"title":"","content":"Yeah; that was a brain fart on my part. Sorry about that.<br /> <br /> The main point I was trying to make, though, is that most Chi Magick Effects don't require a whole lot of successes in and of themselves; most of the work gets done by the Ability that they empower. The biggest exception I've seen to that is the Elements one; and even there, the Effect only needs to generate successes for the <i>additional</i> damage it does; not for the <i>total</i> damage done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-11-2023, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T19:53:12-07:00","id":1520426,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I still don\u2019t get why Chi Flight is regarded as being so problematic. It asks for a Quintessence point to be spent; is there a reason we don\u2019t just lower the Difficulty of the Arete roll by 1, just like the typical effects of Quintessence?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the addition of Prime 2 to the effect. The write-up is specific about how the effect can be achieved without Prime. However, all these chi feats are coming from within a specific paradigm, or a set of similar specific paradigms. We can build whatever limitations we want into a paradigm, can\u2019t we? So, the chi mage\u2019s paradigm says that only masters (defined by having Prime 2) can fly, and that flight doesn\u2019t work without manipulating chi. Manipulating chi is Prime 2 (because that\u2019s Quintessence) so they build that into this effect to satisfy their paradigm. Looks okay to me. Probably part of these mages\u2019 journeys to ascension would involve realising that manipulating chi is not necessary for this at all, just as other aspects of paradigm change along the way.<br /> <br /> (Which doesn\u2019t mean that all Feats of Focussed Chi work just as well, but I\u2019d have to examine the details of each to venture an opinion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T20:08:56-07:00","id":1520427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, all these chi feats are coming from within a specific paradigm, or a set of similar specific paradigms. </div> </div> </div>This is the problem. To many Mage fans, Effects in HDYDT shouldn't be written up with a particular Focus in mind; they should be written up in terms of what they accomplish, and the individual mage should be free to assign whatever Focal requirements best fit their view of how Magick works. By phrasing everything in terms of channeling Chi, HDYDT implicitly assumes that the various Effects in this section are only usable by someone who uses Energy as an Instrument; and also that they're using Martial Arts as a Practice. <br /> <br /> In particular, the text in HDYDT which says, in brief \u201cthis can be accomplished using just Forces \u2022\u2022; but esoteric martial artists make things more complicated than they need to be\u201d rubs a lot of people the wrong way. If you're going to include Prime \u2022\u2022 and Life \u2022\u2022 in an Effect that can be accomplished using just Forces \u2022\u2022, you really ought to get something more out of it. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T22:08:11-07:00","id":1520432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520427#post1520427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the problem. To many Mage fans, Effects in HDYDT shouldn't be written up with a particular Focus in mind; they should be written up in terms of what they accomplish, and the individual mage should be free to assign whatever Focal requirements best fit their view of how Magick works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think it\u2019s really useful to have examples in the context of their paradigms. That\u2019s among the things I\u2019d most want to show to new players (or even old players coming into my game, as experienced players can have wildly varying expectations and I want to manage those expectations) so that they can see how it all fits together.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s too bad that some fans don\u2019t have a supplement that gives them what they want, but I can see why HDTDT followed fairly quickly after the publication of a new core book.<br /> <br /> (And while many effects are written up for specific foci, I don\u2019t agree that there\u2019s any implication that similar can\u2019t be done, tailored for a different focus.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T05:48:00-07:00","id":1520440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520432#post1520432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I think it\u2019s really useful to have examples in the context of their paradigms. That\u2019s among the things I\u2019d most want to show to new players (or even old players coming into my game, as experienced players can have wildly varying expectations and I want to manage those expectations) so that they can see how it all fits together.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s too bad that some fans don\u2019t have a supplement that gives them what they want, but I can see why HDTDT followed fairly quickly after the publication of a new core book.<br /> <br /> (And while many effects are written up for specific foci, I don\u2019t agree that there\u2019s any implication that similar can\u2019t be done, tailored for a different focus.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that this goes against much of how mage has been set up to function.<br /> <br /> There is a clear distinction between set between Focus, and the Spheres. The Mage's spheres demonstrate what it is that a mage is capable of producing theoretically. These are the depths of their effects, what elements of reality they have within the purview of their manipulation. These are stratified in a way which is not context dependent, for example, if you do not have Time 3, you cannot reverse time, if you do not have Prime 1, you cannot hold more than your avatar's level of quintessence, and you cannot cross the gauntlet by sidestepping without Spirit. It is true that you can achieve similar ends via alternative spheres, but that is not what I am describing here. The point is that each rank of a spheres enables you access to specific acts of manipulation.<br /> <br /> When it comes to conjunctive effects, this property holds true. Effects that your mage casts that call on multiple spheres do so because each element of that effect requires that level of the sphere to pull off. If you wish to transform a flower into a in to a crystalline flower, for example, this would require Life 2 for manipulation of plants, and Matter 2 for transmutation of substances into other substances. If you wish to make a portal into an Horizon world chantry, then you would need Spirit 4 to make the portal that goes in to the umbra, and Correspondence 4 to make the portal link to locations that are otherwise no where near each other.<br /> <br /> Each sphere in a conjunctive effect contributes something to the original effect which that sphere alone would otherwise be too limited to do.<br /> <br /> Focus instead isn't a question of what the spheres allow, but on what the mage believes is possible within the boundaries of their spheres. Let us take Forces as an example. Depending on what the mage believes Forces to be will influence the kinds of effects that they believe Forces can do. Let us begin with Forces 2 for minor influences.<br /> <br /> A Verbena style mage may see forces as the elements, Fire, Earth, Water, and Wind. For them, Forces 2 would be about moving fire, influencing the flow of water, Causing termmors in the earth or enforcing great gusts of wind. Their magic would be very much based around the interaction of these elemental forces and as such the effects they work on would be tied in some way to these for areas. Flight for them would be a means of imbuing themselves with wind, Gravity may be a product of Earth, Heat is a force of Fire, cold if a force of Water, but they are inherently linked such that the mage would be able to draw heat from fire, draw cold from water, draw flight from wind, and it would not be seen as a transmutation for them, which would otherwise require Forces 3. However, turning heat in to cold would indeed be a form of Transmutation, they are changing one elemental force in to another elemental force, and so they would not see it possible at that level of the sphere.<br /> <br /> A hermetic mage instead may see each Force as a specific Form from the astral plain, given concrete physical properties via perception. There is a Form of light, a Form of darkness, a Form of Attraction, a Form of Repulsion, a Form of heat, a Form of fire, a Form of cold, a form of movement... All of these forms are distinct and separate Force's patterns, and as such each one is subject to manipulations via Forces 2 on their own terms and independently from one another. It makes sense to the Hermetic that they can move shadow about as this is just manipulating the Form of darkness, while the above mentioned Verbena would have trouble seeing how this would be possible. They might instead consider that darkness is something that is imbued within water, and so the properties of darkness can be manipulated directly by making it flow more like water. However, to the Hermetic, the forms are absolute unto themselves, and as such to make darkness flow like water would be to transform one form in to another form, so they would require Forces 3 to attain a similar feet.<br /> <br /> A Etherite instead may theorise that all forces are simply manifestations of energy, and that this energy is come in a number of difference Qualia. They might recognise a Qualia of Heat, where high energy is warm and low energy is cold. A Qualia of light where darkness is the absence, a Qualia of Plasmic, where high energy plasmic is Electricity, and low energy plasmic if friction, etc. To them Changing the qualia up and down the scale of high to low is about either introducing or removing more of the correct qualia of energy to the equation. And so for them all Forces 2 effects is about manipulating the energy levels within qualia. But Forces 3 would be require to convert one qualia into another qualia.<br /> <br /> But the point here is that these are all still Forces effects. The Verbena does not need Matter to affect water, wind, or earth associated Forces, the Hermetic does not need Mind to focus on the Forms of the astral plane, and the Etherite does not need Prime in order to influence energy levels of the various Qualia.<br /> <br /> Forces covers this, and it is something that the writeup for Chi magic seems to disregard. Each sphere within a conjunctional effect must contribute something to the effect itself in a manner which makes sense for what that sphere is known to do. If the only reason a sphere is used is because it better fits in with their belief and does not actually change the effect itself, then this conflates Focus and Spheres in a way many find contradictory to the established logic.<br /> <br /> This is why I have come up with this interpretation, it demonstrates a role that Prime 2 actually provides for Chi effects in a way that not only makes the sphere use less arbitrary, but also opens the door for Chi using mages to better emulate the areas of the genre from which the practice was inspired. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To sum up: The spheres should dictate what effects are possible from a gameplay persepctive, the Focus should dictates which effects within those spheres the mage believes they can do, and how they must go about them to achieve them.<br /> <br /> Focus should not make certain spheres mandatory, but they can enable more options that better fit the &quot;genre&quot; of the mage who has said Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T13:36:35-07:00","id":1520471,"title":"","content":"Excellent explanation. However, manipulation of forces is Forces 2, not 3. Doesn't matter your paradigm. So, the Verbena, the Hermetic and the Etherite only need Forces 2 to move shadows, considering they can somehow fit into their paradigm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T14:39:23-07:00","id":1520474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520471#post1520471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent explanation. However, manipulation of forces is Forces 2, not 3. Doesn't matter your paradigm. So, the Verbena, the Hermetic and the Etherite only need Forces 2 to move shadows, considering they can somehow fit into their paradigm</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s sort of the point though, in my example, the Hermetic sees darkness and flow as two completely seperate Forms, and as such separate forces entirely, so just as they would need Forces 3 to convert light in to fire, they would need Forces 3 to convert darkness in to flow.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T17:43:40-07:00","id":1520488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520440#post1520440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I have come up with this interpretation, it demonstrates a role that Prime 2 actually provides for Chi effects in a way that not only makes the sphere use less arbitrary, but also opens the door for Chi using mages to better emulate the areas of the genre from which the practice was inspired.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not a fan of adding Spheres into effects for nothing at all. (Sphere ratings are not really an in-setting thing anyway. The character would usually be thinking \u201cI need to reduce my weight\u201d rather than \u201cI need to include Life 2\u201d; Life 2 is just the game system representation of a set of abilities that will tend to develop together because they are related and of similar difficulty. Just like how real people don\u2019t have one of five levels of strength, with everybody with the same number of dots having exactly the same lifting capability, and even when people have similar overall levels of physical strength one may bench more, while another may have higher grip strength. Reality is more complex than game systems. But I digress\u2026)<br /> <br /> But we can have effects that do things on a scale that doesn\u2019t show up in the game system. A basic damaging effect done with coincidental Life and coincidental Matter have exactly the same result in system terms (and if the players rolls exactly one success, these will inflict 0 dice of damage - but that doesn\u2019t mean the effect necessarily does nothing at all). Or look up-thread at my preferred resolution of self-healing as simple feat vs standard feat: self-healing a paper cut still requires Life 2, despite not restoring a health level. Chi Flight\u2019s use of Life 2 is itself an example of this, with the flight being possible with just Forces 2 but Life 2 making changes to how that flight works that show up as nothing more than how we would describe it.<br /> <br /> In the post where I said I don\u2019t really see why Chi Flight is such an issue, I pointed out that Prime 2 in the effect is having an effect. It \u201cchannels the chi force (Quintessence)\u201d - that\u2019s moving Quintessence, a Prime effect. It\u2019s not moving enough Quintessence to show up as anybody or anything gaining or losing a full point of Quintessence (not counting spending a point elsewhere in the effect, because spending Quintessence is possible without Prime) but as I point out in the previous paragraph, the effect doesn\u2019t have to be great enough to show up in system terms to count. (You could possibly make an argument that channelling Quintessence is actually Prime 3, but given an effect below what shows up mechanically, I can see why they decided to be generous.)<br /> <br /> I understand that you would like to see a mechanical difference associated with the addition of Prime 2 into the Chi Flight effect (and as you want that, making up a new game mechanic is reasonable - it\u2019s not my place to tell you that your goal is wrong, although I might have things to say about the effects of your implementation) but nothing in the written rules says that there has to be a mechanic associated with the inclusion of a sphere in an effect; it can just be at the level of description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520440#post1520440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To sum up: The spheres should dictate what effects are possible from a gameplay persepctive, the Focus should dictates which effects within those spheres the mage believes they can do, and how they must go about them to achieve them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if the mage believes they can only do effects that include channelling chi (even if only a tiny amount of it, much less than a single point of Quintessence)? Or perhaps that they can only do certain effects when they also include channelling chi? Or they believe that channeling chi is part of how they must go about achieving certain effects?<br /> <br /> Frankly, if a player tells me they want to add Prime 2 to basically everything their character does to represent channelling chi, I\u2019m not going to fight them on that. They\u2019re setting up a milestone for their character on the path to ascension - learning that channelling chi is not necessary for many effects - and I\u2019d be looking to include that story beat in the chronicle at some point down the track.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520440#post1520440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each sphere within a conjunctional effect must contribute something to the effect itself in a manner which makes sense for what that sphere is known to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don\u2019t think HDYDT\u2019s Chi Flight actually violates that principle, I think it\u2019s worth challenging this assumption. Can you find anywhere in the rules that actually states this?<br /> <br /> BTW, Saikou, I think it would be unwise to assume that just because someone disagrees with your conclusions, they don\u2019t understand the basics of the game system. You wrote an awful lot of words describing in great detail something that really isn\u2019t being disputed by anyone (arguments about Forces 2 vs Forces 3 in specific examples aside).<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T17:47:23-07:00","id":1520489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if the mage believes they can only do effects that include channelling chi (even if only a tiny amount of it, much less than a single point of Quintessence)? </div> </div> </div>That's covered by the Energy Instrument. No need to bring Prime into the picture unless it has a d direct role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T18:45:15-07:00","id":1520495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520489#post1520489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's covered by the Energy Instrument. No need to bring Prime into the picture unless it has a d direct role.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the very same Energy Instrument that says it focuses Quintessence-based magick \u201c[f]or mages with the Prime sphere\u201d, pretty directly bringing Prime into the picture.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also not bothered if the system has several ways to represent very similar things. Maybe one mage shades things one way by incorporating Prime 2 into a bunch of effects, another uses the Energy instrument alone, and a third uses both.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T22:42:31-07:00","id":1520502,"title":"","content":"Also, literal shower thoughts\u2026 Channelling Quintessence is a magickal feat. No instrument can perform a magickal feat without being combined with Spheres to make a magickal effect. (Even if the feat is purely descriptive with no associated game mechanics.)<br /> <br /> So if a mage is channelling Quintessence to achieve something - even as an instrument - Prime should be involved.<br /> <br /> And a mage with Prime can verify whether they actually channel Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T00:47:23-07:00","id":1520505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520488#post1520488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not a fan of adding Spheres into effects for nothing at all. (Sphere ratings are not really an in-setting thing anyway. The character would usually be thinking \u201cI need to reduce my weight\u201d rather than \u201cI need to include Life 2\u201d; Life 2 is just the game system representation of a set of abilities that will tend to develop together because they are related and of similar difficulty. Just like how real people don\u2019t have one of five levels of strength, with everybody with the same number of dots having exactly the same lifting capability, and even when people have similar overall levels of physical strength one may bench more, while another may have higher grip strength. Reality is more complex than game systems. But I digress\u2026)<br /> <br /> But we can have effects that do things on a scale that doesn\u2019t show up in the game system. A basic damaging effect done with coincidental Life and coincidental Matter have exactly the same result in system terms (and if the players rolls exactly one success, these will inflict 0 dice of damage - but that doesn\u2019t mean the effect necessarily does nothing at all). Or look up-thread at my preferred resolution of self-healing as simple feat vs standard feat: self-healing a paper cut still requires Life 2, despite not restoring a health level. Chi Flight\u2019s use of Life 2 is itself an example of this, with the flight being possible with just Forces 2 but Life 2 making changes to how that flight works that show up as nothing more than how we would describe it.<br /> <br /> In the post where I said I don\u2019t really see why Chi Flight is such an issue, I pointed out that Prime 2 in the effect is having an effect. It \u201cchannels the chi force (Quintessence)\u201d - that\u2019s moving Quintessence, a Prime effect. It\u2019s not moving enough Quintessence to show up as anybody or anything gaining or losing a full point of Quintessence (not counting spending a point elsewhere in the effect, because spending Quintessence is possible without Prime) but as I point out in the previous paragraph, the effect doesn\u2019t have to be great enough to show up in system terms to count. (You could possibly make an argument that channelling Quintessence is actually Prime 3, but given an effect below what shows up mechanically, I can see why they decided to be generous.)<br /> <br /> I understand that you would like to see a mechanical difference associated with the addition of Prime 2 into the Chi Flight effect (and as you want that, making up a new game mechanic is reasonable - it\u2019s not my place to tell you that your goal is wrong, although I might have things to say about the effects of your implementation) but nothing in the written rules says that there has to be a mechanic associated with the inclusion of a sphere in an effect; it can just be at the level of description.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if the mage believes they can only do effects that include channelling chi (even if only a tiny amount of it, much less than a single point of Quintessence)? Or perhaps that they can only do certain effects when they also include channelling chi? Or they believe that channeling chi is part of how they must go about achieving certain effects?<br /> <br /> Frankly, if a player tells me they want to add Prime 2 to basically everything their character does to represent channelling chi, I\u2019m not going to fight them on that. They\u2019re setting up a milestone for their character on the path to ascension - learning that channelling chi is not necessary for many effects - and I\u2019d be looking to include that story beat in the chronicle at some point down the track.<br /> <br /> <br /> While I don\u2019t think HDYDT\u2019s Chi Flight actually violates that principle, I think it\u2019s worth challenging this assumption. Can you find anywhere in the rules that actually states this?<br /> <br /> BTW, Saikou, I think it would be unwise to assume that just because someone disagrees with your conclusions, they don\u2019t understand the basics of the game system. You wrote an awful lot of words describing in great detail something that really isn\u2019t being disputed by anyone (arguments about Forces 2 vs Forces 3 in specific examples aside).<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>On your last point, I would like to make something clear. My default is to try and have no assumptions of the person I am speaking to what so ever, this means not assuming that something is taken for granted as understood. This is why I explain my viewpoint out in such detail, so anyone, regardless of their interpretation or their familiarity with the rule, can understand my point of view. It is not a comment on how little I think you understand the system, but a means to fully express my thoughts in as accessible a format as possible.<br /> <br /> now, there is something of a contradiction in what you say. You state you are not a fan on spheres being added to an effect that contribute nothing at all, but at the same time state you are fine with spheres being added which do nothing noticeable. Gameplay wise, this is functionally the same thing, as if a sphere is not contributing to the effect at all.<br /> <br /> I think it is a bit disingenuous to say an effect that rolls zero successes has the same output as any other effect that rolls zero, simply because this is an example not of the effect, but of not casting an effect. It fees like arguing that not climbing a mountain is the same thing as not buying a doughnut. In literal description it is since the effect is you don\u2019t do a thing, but such a statement can be so broadly applied as to be rendered meaningless and unhelpful.<br /> <br /> Especially since if we are looking at a Life effect vs a matter effect when it comes to damage, the Life effect would be targeting the person, while the matter effect would be targeting their clothes or equipment, that alone would be a difference, and even a single success would reflect in that, either in their clothing becoming slightly worn or discoloured, or their body suddenly feeling a bit achey. <br /> <br /> regarding the Forces 2 Life 2 effect for flight, I disagree that it should be identical to the Forces effect alone. Forces 2 alone would affect the area as a whole in regards to gravity, letting you do your jump (as well as anyone else in the area) extra successes could also be used to affect the area you plan to land, assuming nothing bounces you off course (and again, others would feel the effects of such gravity manipultion)<br /> <br /> changing your weight in addition to this would first of all be a part of the effect that only applied to you, and second would allow you to land easily without needing to set up another patch of low gravity where you desired to jump to. Better still, you could land on quite delicate things such as tree branches and paper doors, and the impact of your foot against them would not cause them to break.<br /> <br /> the Life effect does indeed change the nature of the whole effect.<br /> <br /> going back to your point of \u201cprime 2 is needed to channel Chi essence\u201d I state here that one should not let focus dictate which spheres are required to do any basic effect.<br /> <br /> chi healing would be the go to example. It states outright that Chi healing is the same thing as Life 2/3 healing, but \u201cbecause it involves energy\u201d you must add Prime 2 and also spend a point of quintessence for your trouble.<br /> this goes a bit beyond requiring an extra sphere which does nothing, but actually requires an extra sphere which makes the effect more expensive (a point of quintessence) for no actual gain. You are essentially being punished for using chi to do something that not using chi would have allowed with less expenditure. And all of this comes across as the writer basically saying \u201cif you believe in chi, all magic you do must now cost quintessence, so Prime is now mandatory for you to follow your practice properly\u201d and that isn\u2019t a great feel.<br /> <br /> it is why I describe my approach on a bit of spirit. The shaman with just Forces can influence the spirits of the elements like most other Forces mages, even if they are doing so by channeling the elemental spirits to move fore about. However, if they add Spirit 2 to the effect, they can also open up a direct line of communication with said elemental spirit while they are channeling them. This means they can simultaneously direct the fire and discuss with the spirit how they wish the fire to behave, resulting in the fire moving in ways that Forces 2 alone would not be able to manage, and would last far longer than the end of the effect, since once the mage is done, the spirit can keep going.<br /> <br /> if you want to encourage your players choosing to put barriers up against which effects they have access to, I highly recommend you use the system of Practice and Instruments to do this, such that they cannot work on the self, for example, unless they learn how to meditate as is in line with their paradigm, or that they can\u2019t make the gun without getting to the correct level of hypertech first.<br /> <br /> if, however, they insist on wanting a specific sphere before they can access a specific power they already have access to (say, Spirit to converse with the spirits of nature for their Forces effect) then give them the benefit of the conjunctional effect similar to how I have described, not only is it thematically appropriate, but it makes the struggle all the more rewarding as it allows the mage not just to get access to base effects, but to actually explore the full implications of their paradigm by attaining this level of attainment with the sphere which seems prominent in their practice. And it does so in a much better way that simply telling them \u201cwell, you\u2019re a shaman with Spirit 1, therefore you can\u2019t do Forces effects, even with your 3 dots of Forces\u201d<br /> <br /> and unless you plan to fast track them getting the levels of Spirit required, thereby undermining the entire drama of said struggle, it is not really fun to be a mage who can\u2019t use any of the spheres they got at character creation just because \u201ctheir paradigm means their sphere load out is no longer viable\u201d<br /> i would highly discourage this mode of play.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T03:14:22-07:00","id":1520509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520505#post1520505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">now, there is something of a contradiction in what you say. You state you are not a fan on spheres being added to an effect that contribute nothing at all, but at the same time state you are fine with spheres being added which do nothing noticeable. Gameplay wise, this is functionally the same thing, as if a sphere is not contributing to the effect at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t say nothing noticeable. I said \u201cdoesn\u2019t show up in the game system\u201d. Effects which are too minor to be represented mechanically can certainly still be observed by the characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520505#post1520505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is a bit disingenuous to say an effect that rolls zero successes</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t say anything about zero successes. I wrote about 0 dice of damage. That\u2019s the result of 1 success on a basic damaging effect (when cast with most spheres capable of inflicting damage directly, including Life and Matter). And 0 dice of damage does not mean that the effect itself failed. Just as a basic Life healing effect with 1 success can heal a paper cut, a basic Life damaging effect might inflict a paper cut (or something similarly incapacitating); and that would be noticeable by the characters, despite not be represented in the game system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520505#post1520505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since if we are looking at a Life effect vs a matter effect when it comes to damage, the Life effect would be targeting the person, while the matter effect would be targeting their clothes or equipment, that alone would be a difference, and even a single success would reflect in that, either in their clothing becoming slightly worn or discoloured, or their body suddenly feeling a bit achey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly my point. Even with no game mechanical difference, the effect is observably different to the characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520505#post1520505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">going back to your point of \u201cprime 2 is needed to channel Chi essence\u201d I state here that one should not let focus dictate which spheres are required to do any basic effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can state this, but again, I challenge you to find where the rules state this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520505#post1520505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">chi healing would be the go to example. It states outright that Chi healing is the same thing as Life 2/3 healing, but \u201cbecause it involves energy\u201d you must add Prime 2 and also spend a point of quintessence for your trouble. this goes a bit beyond requiring an extra sphere which does nothing, but actually requires an extra sphere which makes the effect more expensive (a point of quintessence) for no actual gain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily no gain. This brings us back to my question of why we aren\u2019t applying the -1 difficulty which is the standard benefit of spending Quintessence on an effect. (Even if you use your system of pre-cast spells attached to Quintessence points, the day may still arise when the pre-cast healing has all been used up, and the characters wants to access just regular healing on the spot, and I\u2019d still wonder why that case isn\u2019t getting -1 difficulty.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520505#post1520505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it does so in a much better way that simply telling them \u201cwell, you\u2019re a shaman with Spirit 1, therefore you can\u2019t do Forces effects, even with your 3 dots of Forces\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven\u2019t suggested that I would tell them anything like that.<br /> <br /> The players get to make choices, and most especially they make choices about their characters. It\u2019s my job to help them understand the consequences of those choices, often (especially before the start of play) before they commit to those choices. Letting somebody create a shaman character and then springing that restriction on them is not fair play by a GM. It wouldn\u2019t be fair play even if it was up to me to build their Foci - and it\u2019s not. These things are tools in the toolbox for players to use, with my guidance.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also my job to negotiate with all of them such that the resulting characters can work well in a game together - and that usually requires a certain form of balance, in which each character has strengths in some situations and weaknesses in others, no two characters\u2019s strengths and weaknesses line up so that one is strictly better than another or consistently outshines the other in ways that matter to the game, and I can reasonably provide situations that allow each character in turn to be spotlighted appropriately. The more options we have for customising Foci, the easier it will be to do this.<br /> <br /> So, I might have a player say, \u201cI\u2019m a shaman with Spirit 1, requiring Spirit 3 to achieve my Forces effects,\u201d but if I do, I\u2019m going to query them about what they are trying to achieve with this character, because I doubt I can hold every PC back to a similar extent and still help other players achieve their visions. (Maybe the player has good reason to do this. I\u2019ve implemented some very odd characters over the years, knowing that my build worked towards some specific thing.) But it\u2019s far more likely that a player will say, \u201cI\u2019m a shaman with Spirit 2, and I build Spirit into all my Forces effects because the spirits must always be invoked to draw upon the powers of the elements,\u201d and I will then advise that this means these effects may sometimes be inaccessible - say when in a place that is cut off from the spirit world, as may be the case in certain Technocracy strongholds - and check whether the player is still cool with it. And then I would work with the other players to ensure that they too have some circumstances in which their characters will be constrained, but I\u2019d go easier on the shaman because they\u2019ve already got a limitation.<br /> <br /> And the same goes for a Chi-manipulating martial artist mage. That player may have chosen to have to spend Quintessence for many effects, but their character may also be the only one whose Focus is appropriate for using the rule allowing an attack to provide magick (in the Magic and Violence section).<br /> <br /> Many starting characters have Spirit 2, Prime 2, or Mind 3 already when these spheres are of central importance to the character, so for these types of characters the requirement to use one of these spheres in most or even all effects is often very minor. And even then, it\u2019s the players\u2019 choice, not mine. I\u2019d love to see a player come up with an alternative implementation of a chi-manipulator martial artist, one who doesn\u2019t believe that chi and Quintessence are the same thing, for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T04:45:50-07:00","id":1520513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520509#post1520509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn\u2019t say nothing noticeable. I said \u201cdoesn\u2019t show up in the game system\u201d. Effects which are too minor to be represented mechanically can certainly still be observed by the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either the effect does something or the effect fizzles and does nothing. My example there of clothing being tattered can be mechanically represented by the difficulty for further attempts at damaging the clothing to be a little easier, similarly making someone feel unwell could lead to a increase in difficulty for their actions. This is very much up to the ST as the ST can simply rule that 1 success on a damage roll is not enough and the effect simply does nothing, but if they wished to make it amount to something anyway, these would be one of the ways to go about it, a small little thing that wouldn't last too long, but could indeed be represented mechanically.<br /> <br /> And when you come down to it, almost anything can be represented mechanically if the ramifications are considered enough. Changing your eye colour could be enough to distract someone while talking to them, allowing your an Appearance roll to catch them off guard. Similarly giving someone a paper cut would give them a +1 diff to any tasks that require pain free precision with whatever part of them the cut was in, and healing it would remove this.<br /> <br /> How micro-managey you wish to be with this stuff is of course a matter of taste, but the point remains, anything can be mechanically represented with enough consideration, and this goes for magic doubly so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520509#post1520509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn\u2019t say anything about zero successes. I wrote about 0 dice of damage. That\u2019s the result of 1 success on a basic damaging effect (when cast with most spheres capable of inflicting damage directly, including Life and Matter). And 0 dice of damage does not mean that the effect itself failed. Just as a basic Life healing effect with 1 success can heal a paper cut, a basic Life damaging effect might inflict a paper cut (or something similarly incapacitating); and that would be noticeable by the characters, despite not be represented in the game system.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As stated above, this is a matter of ST fiat, RAW the effect simply doe no damage, especially as it is stated on pg 502 that effects which affect someone or something else require at least two successes. So a damage effect with only 1 success simply does nothing, though you have the option to roll arete again next turn at +1 diff to build the effect (as stated in pg503 and detailed in pg537. You may feel free to rule this differently, but the intent is for it to fizzle, as is directly stated from pg 546<br /> <br /> to quote &quot;A failed roll - that is, one that scores fewer successes than needed in order to activate the Effect - Fizzles or fades away. If you are using the Degrees of Success chart, the spell might wind up having a diminished result; in most cases, though, the magick just won't manifest.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520509#post1520509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly my point. Even with no game mechanical difference, the effect is observably different to the characters.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There will still be in game ramifications which can still be represented mechanically, but I'm just reiterating the same point now. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520509#post1520509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can state this, but again, I challenge you to find where the rules state this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly thought I did, but to remove all doubt, I will simply quote the entire section in HDYDT pg65<br /> <br /> &quot;Chi Healing<br /> Life-energies, obviously, can heal wounds. And so - using Life 2 for himself and Life 3 for other characters - a skilled chi-based martial artist may use those energies to repair injuries and cure illness. Story-wise, this feat uses special techniques (massage, concentration, advanced acupuncture, and so forth) to redirect the chi flow and heal the injured party. System-wise, this is a basic healing Effect - Life 2 to heal ones self, Life 3 to heal others, and so on; see Body Magick on the Common Magickal Effects chart for details. Because this feat employs chi, the healer must add Prime 2 in order to infuse the wounded character with energy and then direct that energy in aways that do the most good. In order to heal bashing or lethal damage, the healer must spend one Quintessence point per healing attempt. As described in the Magickal Healing entry of the Health and Injury section of Mage 20 (Chapter nine, p.409), it costs one Quintessence point per health level in order to repair aggravated damage. If the healing is essentially invisible, this technique remains coincidental. If the practitioner uses a few touches or needles to cure cancer or close up gaping wounds, the feat becomes vulgar outside of places whose reality accepts that sort of thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> The above clearly states that Life magic is what the effect actually is, and Prime is simply needed &quot;because using Chi&quot; and the only difference between this and the Life rote is &quot;you need to spend quint to do it now&quot;.<br /> <br /> The only reason one would use the quint costing effect over the free version is if you had to lock away Life 2/3 healing effects from easter energy using mages, telling them it is impossible to do this effect unless they have Prime and spend quintessence. And that is the very thing I have been advocating against ruling.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520509#post1520509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily no gain. This brings us back to my question of why we aren\u2019t applying the -1 difficulty which is the standard benefit of spending Quintessence on an effect. (Even if you use your system of pre-cast spells attached to Quintessence points, the day may still arise when the pre-cast healing has all been used up, and the characters wants to access just regular healing on the spot, and I\u2019d still wonder why that case isn\u2019t getting -1 difficulty.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do not understand the problem you site, could you please restate?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520509#post1520509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven\u2019t suggested that I would tell them anything like that.<br /> <br /> The players get to make choices, and most especially they make choices about their characters. It\u2019s my job to help them understand the consequences of those choices, often (especially before the start of play) before they commit to those choices. Letting somebody create a shaman character and then springing that restriction on them is not fair play by a GM. It wouldn\u2019t be fair play even if it was up to me to build their Foci - and it\u2019s not. These things are tools in the toolbox for players to use, with my guidance.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also my job to negotiate with all of them such that the resulting characters can work well in a game together - and that usually requires a certain form of balance, in which each character has strengths in some situations and weaknesses in others, no two characters\u2019s strengths and weaknesses line up so that one is strictly better than another or consistently outshines the other in ways that matter to the game, and I can reasonably provide situations that allow each character in turn to be spotlighted appropriately. The more options we have for customising Foci, the easier it will be to do this.<br /> <br /> So, I might have a player say, \u201cI\u2019m a shaman with Spirit 1, requiring Spirit 3 to achieve my Forces effects,\u201d but if I do, I\u2019m going to query them about what they are trying to achieve with this character, because I doubt I can hold every PC back to a similar extent and still help other players achieve their visions. (Maybe the player has good reason to do this. I\u2019ve implemented some very odd characters over the years, knowing that my build worked towards some specific thing.) But it\u2019s far more likely that a player will say, \u201cI\u2019m a shaman with Spirit 2, and I build Spirit into all my Forces effects because the spirits must always be invoked to draw upon the powers of the elements,\u201d and I will then advise that this means these effects may sometimes be inaccessible - say when in a place that is cut off from the spirit world, as may be the case in certain Technocracy strongholds - and check whether the player is still cool with it. And then I would work with the other players to ensure that they too have some circumstances in which their characters will be constrained, but I\u2019d go easier on the shaman because they\u2019ve already got a limitation.<br /> <br /> And the same goes for a Chi-manipulating martial artist mage. That player may have chosen to have to spend Quintessence for many effects, but their character may also be the only one whose Focus is appropriate for using the rule allowing an attack to provide magick (in the Magic and Violence section).<br /> <br /> Many starting characters have Spirit 2, Prime 2, or Mind 3 already when these spheres are of central importance to the character, so for these types of characters the requirement to use one of these spheres in most or even all effects is often very minor. And even then, it\u2019s the players\u2019 choice, not mine. I\u2019d love to see a player come up with an alternative implementation of a chi-manipulator martial artist, one who doesn\u2019t believe that chi and Quintessence are the same thing, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas if I had a player saying &quot;I;m a shaman with spirit 1, requiring spirit 3 to achieve my Forces effects&quot;, I would explain to them that isn't actually how the game should work, they can still do their forces effects without needing spirit, it just requires that they perform a number of rituals ahead of time to engage in chiminage, essentially thing that can influence the spirits without needing to cross the gauntlet to do so, such that they will sufficiently believe they are able to influence the spirits within the elemental Forces.<br /> <br /> I shall reiterate my stance. The spheres are one thing and they determine what effects are possible. They have a logic and they are very consistent with this logic. Focus determines what the mage must do to achieve their effects, which effects they believe are possible, and may colour some of the ways in which an effect both manifests and resolves, as well as any other moments of fallout such as paradox, resonance, spiritual attraction, or other quirks in reality such as how fate reacts to Entropy.<br /> <br /> I do not believe focus should influence which spheres someone needs to cast the same effect Forces effect<br /> Verbena elementalist should not need Matter to make the wind blow<br /> Virtual Adepts should not need Data to program a breeze<br /> Hermetics should not need Mind to focus their will to conjure a zephyre<br /> Shamans should not need Spirit to call upon the gods of storms to make a wind<br /> Euthanatoi should not need Entropy to request to Shiva to enable fate to cause a wind to blow right now<br /> and Chi mages should not need Prime to focus a burst of air out from their open fist.<br /> <br /> Such a thing conflates the relationship of the spheres and of belief in a way which contradicts the established logic of the spheres.<br /> In a conjunctive effect, any additional sphere must be additive, it must contribute something that the lone sphere would otherwise be unable to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T06:37:33-07:00","id":1520519,"title":"","content":"I need to break out smaller bits and ignore some less-important stuff for now. Too little time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520513#post1520513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly thought I did, but to remove all doubt, I will simply quote the entire section in HDYDT pg65</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that bit. This statement: \u201cI state here that one should not let focus dictate which spheres are required to do any basic effect.\u201d I\u2019m challenging that basic assumption. Where do the rules say that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520513#post1520513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not understand the problem you site, could you please restate?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not a problem with your house rule, as such. It\u2019s just that your house rule won\u2019t apply in all situations.<br /> <br /> A chi-using mage starts the day with 3 Quintessence, and hangs 3 effects on them, per your rules. He gets into a big boss-fight alongside the other members of his cabal, and by the time the dust settles he has used all 3 Quintessence. However, he has also absorbed another point of Quintessence along the way. (He\u2019s a Prime-wielding mage. It\u2019s entirely possible for him to have found some way to refresh during a long scene.) One if his cabal-mates got seriously hurt in the fight, though, so he wants to use his Chi Healing to help him. He spends the point of Quintessence, and casts the effect. He gets no benefit out of that pre-casting mechanic, because whatever he had pre-cast had been used previously.<br /> <br /> And I\u2019d be inclined to just let him have -1 difficulty from the Quintessence expenditure. I wonder why others wouldn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520513#post1520513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas if I had a player saying &quot;I;m a shaman with spirit 1, requiring spirit 3 to achieve my Forces effects&quot;, I would explain to them that isn't actually how the game should work,</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a game about characters who shape reality. The game should work in accordance with the player\u2019s vision of their character and their character\u2019s reality, at least to some extent.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s fine for you to explain your alternative for how a shaman\u2019s magic might work, but I intend to listen to my players and find out why they build the Foci they do.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T07:39:02-07:00","id":1520521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520474#post1520474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s sort of the point though, in my example, the Hermetic sees darkness and flow as two completely seperate Forms, and as such separate forces entirely, so just as they would need Forces 3 to convert light in to fire, they would need Forces 3 to convert darkness in to flow.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What you mean by flow? Movement? Moving shadows should be Forces 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T07:58:47-07:00","id":1520524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520488#post1520488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don\u2019t think HDYDT\u2019s Chi Flight actually violates that principle, I think it\u2019s worth challenging this assumption. Can you find anywhere in the rules that actually states this?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you..Are you really asking for evidence that you only add spheres that contribute to the effect? Well, it's in every mage core book in the step-by-step guides for how to do magick. Also, it's only intuitive. Why the hell would someone add a sphere into an effect that has nothing to contribute?<br /> <br /> Instruments were <b>never</b> a factor to determine which spheres to use, only the result itself. That was added in HDYDT and that's the main reason this book is so criticized.<br /> <br /> One more point, the player can add all the fluff he wants, without adding spheres. You want to heal someone, but you want to make it in a flash of light. You don't need Forces. You only need Life (for healing) and add the fluff from the instruments. The player can choose how their magick looks like, things like Resonance help into that. Those, however have no mechanical importance, and thus do not add any sphere to the effect.<br /> <br /> If your player want to use energy, he doesn't need to add Prime 2 in healing (for example), since Prime 2 wouldn't be doing anything in the effect. Just make him explain how the instrument work. Restricting an instrument (energy) to a sphere is not how M20 foci works. I know that they made a terrible description of some instruments, though and energy is probably the worst...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T08:25:09-07:00","id":1520526,"title":"","content":"Also, don't take any of this as an attack on how <i>you</i> handle it. If you want to mandate Prime 2 in order to use the Energy Instrument and that works for you, go for it! It doesn't match the way the rules are written in the core book; but that's fine. I'm a big fan of house rules, even extremely minor ones such as letting (or even insisting that) players include Spheres in their Effects for strictly Focal reasons, even if they have no impact on what the Effect does. It's not a house rule that <i>I</i> use, which is why I appreciate suggestions about how such Spheres might actually make a meaningful contribution to the Effect. But you do you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-13-2023, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T15:46:31-07:00","id":1520552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520519#post1520519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to break out smaller bits and ignore some less-important stuff for now. Too little time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not that bit. This statement: \u201cI state here that one should not let focus dictate which spheres are required to do any basic effect.\u201d I\u2019m challenging that basic assumption. Where do the rules say that?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, Let's got back to M20 core, pg 528<br /> <br /> Step One: Effect<br /> <br /> &quot;Spheres: The Foundation of Each Effect<br /> Practically speaking, a sphere determines what your character can do. In a broader sense, the Spheres reflect your character's knowledge about the metaphysical forces he employs. When you're determining what you can do and how you can do it, the Spheres provide the foundation of your abilities. To command fire, for example, you need to have the Forces Sphere.&quot;<br /> <br /> Followed by the next step on pg 529<br /> <br /> Step Two: Ability<br /> <br /> &quot;Does your mage BELIEVE that he can do such things? Sure, maybe you've got Forces 3 and Prime 2 on your character sheet. A blank Suit can't just snap her fingers and make fireballs appear, however. Such feats don't fit her focus - they violate her beliefs. She can't conjure fire using someone else's focus either; if you gave her a rune-carved staff, she'd try to hit someone with it, not summon a firestorm....&quot;<br /> <br /> The order is clear, step one is determine the effect by working around what is possible via your spheres, then step two is see how that effect is possible to do via your Focus. No where is it stated that Focus dictates Spheres.<br /> <br /> In fact, the idea of Focus dictating spheres contradicts other passages of the book, in particular when shedding a focus or working without a focus. Any mage can work without a focus, all they need to do is spend WP and get a +3 on the diff. Instead they can just work with an unfamiliar focus at +2 diff. This means that any mage who has the rigth combination of spheres can, and I quote from the book (pg 566) &quot;Will things to happen without using tools or a practice. Working through determination alone, a mage can suprass her focus and conjure Effects without channeling belief through practice or tools.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, if you dictate that Shaman requires Spirit 2 to do any Forces effects, then this creates a conundrum. If those spheres are required, and the Shaman does not have Spirit 2, then they simply cannot do the effect. Yet if they do have Spirit 2 and they work without their focus, thereby working with will and not via spiritual contact, then what exactly is Spirit 2 contributing to the effect?<br /> <br /> And if you mean to imply that such a shaman may only use Forces alone with they work without a focus, you create a bigger conundrum once we get to shedding instruments. If a shaman sheds the instrument that they rely on to communicate with the spirits, then would, by proxy of adding spirit 2 to every effect, mean they are now able to have an essentially permanent break in difficulty for all spells going forwards? The rules do not cover this, and I believe they don't cover this because such a thing was never the intention throughout the history of mage. I would in fact posit that the Bit of Spirit sidebar and the Chi Healing section as written was an ill-thought out addition which has necessitated re-imagining and reinterpreting in order to maintain the proper logic of the spheres as established.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the book would also have example of will working requiring Mind, Alchemy requiring Matter, Prayer requiring Spirit, body work requiring Life, the Euthanatos requiring Entropy for all things, Virtual Adepts requireing Data for all things, Syndicate requiring Mind for all things, and this simply doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520519#post1520519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not a problem with your house rule, as such. It\u2019s just that your house rule won\u2019t apply in all situations.<br /> <br /> A chi-using mage starts the day with 3 Quintessence, and hangs 3 effects on them, per your rules. He gets into a big boss-fight alongside the other members of his cabal, and by the time the dust settles he has used all 3 Quintessence. However, he has also absorbed another point of Quintessence along the way. (He\u2019s a Prime-wielding mage. It\u2019s entirely possible for him to have found some way to refresh during a long scene.) One if his cabal-mates got seriously hurt in the fight, though, so he wants to use his Chi Healing to help him. He spends the point of Quintessence, and casts the effect. He gets no benefit out of that pre-casting mechanic, because whatever he had pre-cast had been used previously.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>ok...? Not sure why this is an issue. What would happen is if they heal someone ad-hoc, then it's a simple Life effect, with no need to use prime. What I am saying is the use of Prime allows the effect to be preloaded in the quintessence they have stored within them/ their soul gems.<br /> <br /> I would not impose Chi Healing as written outside of the context of having a preloaded effect as I describe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520519#post1520519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I\u2019d be inclined to just let him have -1 difficulty from the Quintessence expenditure. I wonder why others wouldn\u2019t.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You do not need Prime to use Quintessence for the -1 diff to cast. Forcing mages to need Prime to use Quintessence in this way makes Quintessence essentially unusable to non-prime mages. I highly recommend against doing this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520519#post1520519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a game about characters who shape reality. The game should work in accordance with the player\u2019s vision of their character and their character\u2019s reality, at least to some extent.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s fine for you to explain your alternative for how a shaman\u2019s magic might work, but I intend to listen to my players and find out why they build the Foci they do.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are free to throw the book out as much as you like for the sake of your table. Heck you could even scrap the sphere system all together and invent your own base means of magic, I know a number of people who have done just that.<br /> <br /> But we are discussing the book, and the merits of the rules as written and how to interpret them in a way that maintains logical consistency. Which is the entire goal of the idea I have presented here. A means to incorporate the spirit of chi effects which does not contradict the established logic of the spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 08-13-2023, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T17:44:32-07:00","id":1520562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520526#post1520526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to mandate Prime 2 in order to use the Energy Instrument and that works for you, go for it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite what I suggested. What I suggested was requiring Prime 2 when using the Energy instrument <i>to manipulate Quintessence</i>.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t see why you couldn\u2019t create a character who manipulates chi, and considers chi to be a different thing to Quintessence. Also, a character who manipulates energy which is not chi (and not Quintessence). And these energies may or may not be entirely a product of the characters\u2019 paradigms (and so may disappear as the character moves towards Ascension and gains more understanding of the underlying truth of the universe). And all of these characters could exist in a chronicle alongside a Quintessence manipulator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520526#post1520526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't match the way the rules are written in the core book; but that's fine. I'm a big fan of house rules, even extremely minor ones such as letting (or even insisting that) players include Spheres in their Effects for strictly Focal reasons, even if they have no impact on what the Effect does.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, I\u2019m not sure it\u2019s even a house rule. I haven\u2019t spotted anything in M20 that actually says not to do this. It fits with Process Based Determinism, which M20 states in considered to be the default approach by the rules (but not the only approach a group might choose to use). And it seems to be exactly what the designers have done, in Feats of Focussed Chi, and A Little Bit of Spirit, and Elemental Mastery, and probably elsewhere.<br /> <br /> (And if this is the default approach taken by the M20 designers, then I don\u2019t mind those who prefer to do otherwise, of course. But it would be nice to see people not treat those in a different camp as harshly as I have seen.)<br /> <br /> And I\u2019m pretty sure this argument goes back to the days when it was primarily taking place on Usenet. I haven\u2019t scoured the older editions for examples of rotes that seem to include spheres that are more Focus-dependent (and I don\u2019t intend to - when I agreed to run a game for friends, I also declared a canon for the game, and nothing published prior to M20 is in that canon; which means we are all free to use it for inspiration, but are not beholden to it, and nobody has to read large amounts of older material) but it wouldn\u2019t surprise me if there were earlier examples of it somewhere.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T19:30:20-07:00","id":1520568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520562#post1520562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite what I suggested. What I suggested was requiring Prime 2 when using the Energy instrument <i>to manipulate Quintessence</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The catch is that, in order for that to be a thing, you actually need an Effect that manipulates Quintessence. And as Saikou pointed out, that's a decision that gets made <i>before you bring Focus into the picture.</i> Chi-Healing, for example, doesn't manipulate Quintessence; it heals the body. By all rights, it ought to be a straight-up Life Effect. <br /> <br /> And yeah; spending a point of Quintessence can reduce the difficulty of the casting by one. <i>But you don't need Prime to do that. All</i> mages can do that. So what's Prime doing in the Effect? As written, absolutely <i>nothing.</i> Which is why this thread exists: to come up with something that Prime can actually contribute to the Effect. The original suggestion was to enable prep time through Prime; my counter-suggestion was to imbue Magick into the performance of an Ability. What both have in common is that Prime isn't there for flavor; it actually <i>does</i> something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T00:59:02-07:00","id":1520576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520562#post1520562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, I\u2019m not sure it\u2019s even a house rule. I haven\u2019t spotted anything in M20 that actually says not to do this. It fits with Process Based Determinism, which M20 states in considered to be the default approach by the rules (but not the only approach a group might choose to use).</div> </div> </div> </div>Process-Based Determinism is a guideline that exists for the purpose of judging whether an Effect is Vulgar or Coincidental by the rules as written; it has nothing to do with deciding which Spheres are needed for the Effect. Applying it to the choice of Spheres is a house rule, as is applying Focal elements to the decision of what Spheres are necessary.<br /> <br /> And, like I said: if you want to do that, far be it from me to attempt to dissuade you. I even agree with you to an extent on the philosophical level: in practice, I generally don't insist that the players describe what they're trying to accomplish in a result-based manner; I let them describe it initially in a process-based manner. It helps maintain immersion to do it that way. But <i>then</i> I try to \u201cread between the lines\u201d and discern what the intended result is, and then choose the Sphere requirements based off of that; and if I'm unclear as to what they're after, I then ask them to clarify. So even with the player describing the Effect in process-based terms from the beginning, I <i>still</i> end up choosing the Sphere requirements in a results-based manner. This is because you can't to <i>everything</i> according to the process; at <i>some</i> point, you need to figure out what the actual result is intended to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T01:48:20-07:00","id":1520578,"title":"","content":"The flow chart I use goes like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Determine what the effect is supposed to achieve<br /> - know what the player is trying to do to reality<br /> - determine if their spheres enable anything approaching this<br /> - (let player know what range of options for achieving said effect are within their sphere capabilities if necessary)<br /> <br /> 2. Determine how that effect may be made manifest<br /> - Ask player to describe what their mage believes their effect is doing (we skip to this step is which spheres are being used is pre established)<br /> - Consider the internal logic of the character, i.e. what they believe they are doing, and how that would alter/colour the effect<br /> - Discuss with player what within their own focus is required for such an effect to be made manifest (practice/instrument choice)<br /> <br /> 3. Set up the roll<br /> <br /> this is where I start to consider process based determinism<br /> <br /> - Consider based on what the effect does, whether they way it is cast fits in with or violates local reality zone, and if the effect is even observable, whether or not this is coincidental or vulgar, assign diff accordingly<br /> - apply modifiers based on the table<br /> - consider number of successes required to meet the minimum expectations of the effect<br /> - consider if it is possible to \u201ctry again\u201d, how much time is required between rolls, and whether or not a ritual is the only way to go about said effect via their focus.<br /> <br /> 4. Interpret results (assuming threshold successes met)<br /> <br /> This is where process based determinism really gets the focus<br /> <br /> - start with spheres used, this will determine exactly what aspects of reality were affected to bring about the effect.<br /> - next consider mage\u2019s belief, this will determine how said effect manifests, whether it be a spiritual presence, a shift in energies, a sudden shudder, a flurry of petals\u2026 this will affect not only how it looks but also the nature of the effect, healing agg via prayer will look like a soft glow over their body and leave a holy restorative resonance. healing via spirits may attract other spirits to the area, while healing using modern science might be a lengthy process requiring maybe 1-2 days of \u2018casting\u2019<br /> - lastly, consider the instruments used, and the consequences they might have. Healing via prayer would require time and concentration, as well as no interruption in most cases. Healing via the spirits requires the correct offering, with the offering chosen determining what spirit will offer healing, and at what potential price (such as, a water spirit may heal them, but the healed mage may now have an aversion to fire for a while), and healing via medical machinery may require a medicine check to avoid creating short term physical flaws that persist for a short while (or a long while if they botch)<br /> <br /> (some of these points may be better considered at stage 3, especially in terms of time if the mage is going to take multiple rolls to achieve their effect, and they would like the option to abort mid way if it looks like it will take too long.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 08-14-2023, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T06:22:49-07:00","id":1520588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520552#post1520552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No where is it stated that Focus dictates Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pulling this to the top because I think the point I\u2019m about to make is really important.<br /> <br /> Nobody has made a claim that Focus dictates spheres. I have simply been pointing out that the rules do not require that Focus always be ignored when considering spheres - not that I\u2019ve found, anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520552#post1520552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, Let's got back to M20 core, pg 528<br /> <br /> Step One: Effect<br /> <br /> &quot;Spheres: The Foundation of Each Effect<br /> Practically speaking, a sphere determines what your character can do. In a broader sense, the Spheres reflect your character's knowledge about the metaphysical forces he employs. When you're determining what you can do and how you can do it, the Spheres provide the foundation of your abilities. To command fire, for example, you need to have the Forces Sphere.&quot;<br /> <br /> Followed by the next step on pg 529<br /> <br /> Step Two: Ability<br /> <br /> &quot;Does your mage BELIEVE that he can do such things? Sure, maybe you've got Forces 3 and Prime 2 on your character sheet. A blank Suit can't just snap her fingers and make fireballs appear, however. Such feats don't fit her focus - they violate her beliefs. She can't conjure fire using someone else's focus either; if you gave her a rune-carved staff, she'd try to hit someone with it, not summon a firestorm....&quot;<br /> <br /> The order is clear, step one is determine the effect by working around what is possible via your spheres, then step two is see how that effect is possible to do via your Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, first thing to note is that if you are trying to get support from the order of this procedure, obviously you don\u2019t know an <i>explicit</i> statement in the rules to back up the idea that Focus must be kept so distinct from the spheres given for an effect.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I don\u2019t know about you, but when stating my intent in any reasonably freeform system, I\u2019m often inclined to say things like \u201cI call upon the spirits to make the fire dance,\u201d or \u201cI draw chi from the life around me, and channel that energy into my friend to close the wound.\u201d If there\u2019s an observable change (and with Prime, movement of chi/Quintessence is observable) then I think that\u2019s part of the effect.<br /> <br /> And when I get to step 2, I could easily see myself saying, as a player, \u201cWell, no, I don\u2019t believe I can heal; not without manipulating chi/Quintessence, and that isn\u2019t happening here.\u201d And that sends me back to Step 1 to think through my casting again.<br /> <br /> In practice, I think this process is nowhere near as clear-cut as you make it out to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520552#post1520552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, the idea of Focus dictating spheres contradicts other passages of the book, in particular when shedding a focus or working without a focus. Any mage can work without a focus, all they need to do is spend WP and get a +3 on the diff. Instead they can just work with an unfamiliar focus at +2 diff. This means that any mage who has the rigth combination of spheres can, and I quote from the book (pg 566) &quot;Will things to happen without using tools or a practice. Working through determination alone, a mage can suprass her focus and conjure Effects without channeling belief through practice or tools.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So when doing these things just drop the Sphere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520552#post1520552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if you dictate that Shaman requires Spirit 2 to do any Forces effects, then this creates a conundrum. If those spheres are required, and the Shaman does not have Spirit 2, then they simply cannot do the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not dictating anything. Players build their characters. They choose what limitations they build into them (negotiated with me to produce reasonable fairness across the group). I inform them of the consequences of their choices before they are committed to those choices.<br /> <br /> So why do you suppose players will build these characters?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an old joke\u2026 A man walks into his doctor\u2019s office, and says, \u201cDoc, it hurts when I do this.\u201d The doctor replies, \u201cDon\u2019t do that. Next!\u201d<br /> <br /> These types of objections are meaningless. You say problems occur if somebody does some particular, and particularly useless, thing. The solution is that we just don\u2019t do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520552#post1520552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a shaman sheds the instrument that they rely on to communicate with the spirits, then would, by proxy of adding spirit 2 to every effect, mean they are now able to have an essentially permanent break in difficulty for all spells going forwards? The rules do not cover this, and I believe they don't cover this because such a thing was never the intention throughout the history of mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what difficulty break rule are you referring to here? There\u2019s a couple of different ways to reduce difficulty, and I do not know which you are referring to or how it applies.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520552#post1520552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, the book would also have example of will working requiring Mind, Alchemy requiring Matter, Prayer requiring Spirit, body work requiring Life, the Euthanatos requiring Entropy for all things, Virtual Adepts requireing Data for all things, Syndicate requiring Mind for all things, and this simply doesn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no reason that the possibility of effect spheres being affected by the means used to cast the effect would require any of that.<br /> <br /> So, in summary, there\u2019s certainly nothing explicitly stating your position in the rules, and so far I really wouldn\u2019t consider any of your attempts at deducing support from what is in the rules to be conclusive. (Noting that there is one where I\u2019m not sure which rule you are referring to.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520552#post1520552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok...? Not sure why this is an issue. What would happen is if they heal someone ad-hoc, then it's a simple Life effect, with no need to use prime. What I am saying is the use of Prime allows the effect to be preloaded in the quintessence they have stored within them/ their soul gems.<br /> <br /> I would not impose Chi Healing as written outside of the context of having a preloaded effect as I describe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I told you it\u2019s not an issue. I just didn\u2019t assume that adding a new use for Quintessence also meant dropping the Feats of Focussed Chi in their regular context.<br /> <br /> And all I said about that is that I don\u2019t see why we wouldn\u2019t just give -1 difficulty for the Quintessence expenditure if somebody was using that in the usual fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520552#post1520552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not need Prime to use Quintessence for the -1 diff to cast. Forcing mages to need Prime to use Quintessence in this way makes Quintessence essentially unusable to non-prime mages. I highly recommend against doing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never suggested doing that. Prime is required to channel Quintessence, not to spend personal Quintessence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520552#post1520552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we are discussing the book,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not when you\u2019re talking about chiminage, we\u2019re not. I am familiar with that term (having played Werewolf: the Apocalypse a fair bit) but it\u2019s not in the M20 core book at all.<br /> <br /> And sure, the M20 rules are designed to be flexible, and allow you to introduce your vision of shamanism, but that also means there is scope and support for other approaches too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T07:42:03-07:00","id":1520590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520576#post1520576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, like I said: if you want to do that, far be it from me to attempt to dissuade you. I even agree with you to an extent on the philosophical level: in practice, I generally don't insist that the players describe what they're trying to accomplish in a result-based manner; I let them describe it initially in a process-based manner. It helps maintain immersion to do it that way. But <i>then</i> I try to \u201cread between the lines\u201d and discern what the intended result is, and then choose the Sphere requirements based off of that; and if I'm unclear as to what they're after, I then ask them to clarify.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then what if the player is clear in their intent that the effect manipulate chi/Quintessence? It may only be a small part of the effect beside healing health levels or flying or the like, but a small part is still part, and that doesn\u2019t seem like an illegitimate intent (at least not necessarily). Small things like that can be important to how players wish to portray their characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T07:53:27-07:00","id":1520591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520590#post1520590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then what if the player is clear in their intent that the effect manipulate chi/Quintessence? \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIt may only be a small part of the effect beside healing health levels or flying or the like, but a small part is still part, and that doesn\u2019t seem like an illegitimate intent (at least not necessarily). Small things like that can be important to how players wish to portray their characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the Storyteller, I have final say over what Spheres are required. If I deem that what the player is asking for isn't actually doing anything that would require Prime, then I don't require any dots of Prime in order to work the Effect.<br /> <br /> I have never once had a player complain that I didn't require them to use a Sphere that they thought ought to be required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T08:24:49-07:00","id":1520594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody has made a claim that Focus dictates spheres. I have simply been pointing out that the rules do not require that Focus always be ignored when considering spheres - not that I\u2019ve found, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the rules are (and always were) clear that focus is always ignored when considering spheres because the spheres depend <b>only</b> on <b>what</b> the mage is doing from an OOC point of view and not by what means he does it.<br /> <br /> The spheres are determined <b>first</b>, and in that step, foci are never discussed.<br /> After the spheres are determined, you will go on and look for foci and the rest.<br /> <br /> Also, visual effects do not require spheres, it can be added as fluff and Resonance. You don't need Forces to make a &quot;lay on hands&quot; healing that glows a light from your hands.<br /> <br /> Also, process based determinism (PBD) doea not have anything to do with foci. It has to do with choosing what spheres are required based on what process is happening. From the M20 example:<br /> <br /> &quot;Summoning&quot; a cab using PBD (the default rule):<br /> <br /> \u2013 Grab an existing cab: Correspondence 3/Mind 2/Entropy 2 to find and make the taxi go your way (the cab has to be already there, you're just making it go to you)<br /> <br /> \u2013 Create a cab and a driver from thing air: Matter 4/Forces3/Life 5/Mind 5 <br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> - Change the odda of a taxi showing to you with a LOT of successes and big waiting time (of course, you have to be in a city and etc.)<br /> <br /> Now, Result based determinism (RBD) doesn't care for what is happening, just what the result you want, which is going from point A to point B, so:<br /> <br /> -Correspondence 3 to go from A to B and the ST invent some bullshit for that to happen, for example, a taxi happens to appear.<br /> <br /> Note that neither option say anything about foci. You will not find anything on M20, or outside of hdydt, that involves foci into how to determine spheres for an effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T10:54:12-07:00","id":1520686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly what difficulty break rule are you referring to here? There\u2019s a couple of different ways to reduce difficulty, and I do not know which you are referring to or how it applies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to context: The difficulty break that happens when you surpass an Instrument, yet use it ayway. Since Spheres are immaterial, ever present parts of your Character Sheet, and there seems to be a consensus that adding the Sphere has no drawbacks, you could add it all the time.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's that big of a deal. It's an advantage of all Instruments that are &quot;part of the mage&quot;, really. It comes with the fact you can't normaly be caugth flat footed w/o them (like, if your Instrument it's &quot;tought forms&quot; - well, you likely have those as long as you're not unconscious or somehow perturbed) ... altrough using an abstraction that exists mostly on your OOC character sheet, (and thus can <i>never </i>be taken from you?), such as a Sphere, it's a good candidate for &quot;most convinient&quot; - depending on application<br /> <br /> Like, a different thing it's if you use someting that can only be <i>accessed trough </i>magick (such as, talking with specific spirits, who may just not be there even with Spirit 2. Or, &quot;a connection with the Spirit Worlds&quot;, which may require a roll against the Gauntlet if you're not <i>on </i>it)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not dictating anything. Players build their characters. They choose what limitations they build into them (negotiated with me to produce reasonable fairness across the group). I inform them of the consequences of their choices before they are committed to those choices.<br /> <br /> So why do you suppose players will build these characters?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an old joke\u2026 A man walks into his doctor\u2019s office, and says, \u201cDoc, it hurts when I do this.\u201d The doctor replies, \u201cDon\u2019t do that. Next!\u201d<br /> <br /> These types of objections are meaningless. You say problems occur if somebody does some particular, and particularly useless, thing. The solution is that we just don\u2019t do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's so meaningless.<br /> <br /> What does &quot;we just don\u2019t do that&quot; mean?. The implication it's &quot;we don't play a Shaman without Spirit 2&quot;, but that's a case-by-case thing...while I've never played a Shaman w/o Spirit 2, I can imagine psionic-like characters w/o Mind 2 (not all psions are empath/telepath), and I actually favor Martial Artists that understood Chi as the flows of Life rather than the more &quot;energy-like&quot; dupla of Prime/Quintessence<br /> <br /> Really, &quot;we just don\u2019t do that&quot; in this kind of context could easily mean &quot;we just don't use the <i>optional </i>HDYDT rule&quot;. And that's also my posture, altrough I do like your idea for the <i>effects</i>.\u200b<br /> <br /> I actually like the idea of combining the Spheres the way you propose to create particular effects. Like, using Mind 3/Forces 3, instead of Prime 2/Forces 3, to conjure a fire with the power of your emotions or similar (understanding that this will deplete the mage's psyche). But when one says, &quot;psychics use their mind as a Focus, so it HAS to have at least Mind 2&quot;, that's <i>stronger of a claim</i>.<br /> <br /> One could think that implies I would be using it even if I'm NOT actually creating fire with the power of my emotions/psyche, but rather have a more &quot;reality-warper&quot; like approach that uses psionics as explanation, and would be more comfortable by moving Quintessence arround.<br /> <br /> While <b><i>this may not be </i></b><i><b><i>what you mean</i></b>,</i> <b>but </b><i><b>the rule in HDYDT kinda does follow that path. </b></i>As per the rule: <i>assume that a mage whose reality-bending Arts involve her connection to the spiritual essence of the world needs a Spirit Sphere Rank of 2 or better (the Touch Spirit Effect), in addition\u200b...</i><br /> <br /> Note that the Effect it's not called an &quot;Instrument&quot;. This kinda implies I would need to include that element in <i>every effect </i>of <i>every</i> <i>Instrument</i>. It's not suggested that I can, say, chose an Instrument that &quot;it's&quot; Spirit 2, <i>and other that isn't</i> (like, say, medicinal herbs and drugs that may make me closer to the spirit world w/o actually manipulating &quot;spirit essence&quot;). Merely having an Art that <i>involves </i>a connection it's enough<br /> <br /> Heck, the rule itself doesn't allow for<i> less than 2 </i>for perception based effects in HDYDT, or does it?. It does say (in another paragraph) that the requirement could be higher than 2 depending on what are you doing, but, unless I missed something, it doesn't mention it can be <i>lower</i> depending on what you're doing...and<i> kinda says it can't be lower</i> <i>with that</i> &quot;<b><i>2 or better</i></b>&quot;. One could read the rule as actually i<i>ncreasing the base difficulty of all lvl 1 effects in one</i> (and the Paradox on a botch). Altrough a case could be made that that's not the <i>spirit </i>of the rule... <hr /><br /> My take it's to allow effects like those you mention w/o tying them to a rule that demands the use of a &quot;Sphere as a Focus&quot;, potentially enabling them for mages that <i>don't</i> use the Sphere as a Focus, but still have a Focus where that power would make sense (like, say, Euthanatos that have a divinely-oriented Paradigm, don't believe particularly in Chi, but still can hang healing effects arround with divinely-oriented Prime - this use of Prime is actually canon for the Euthanatos, well,<i> kinda</i>: Search for the &quot;Gift of Prana&quot; rote).<br /> <br /> That being said, I think Dataweaver's idea of shamans using &quot;Focus Spirit 2&quot; rolling against the Gauntlet it's cool and thematic. I like it and see it as a good case to <i>allow </i>the optional rule on some special cases\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-15-2023, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T17:05:02-07:00","id":1520723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody has made a claim that Focus dictates spheres. I have simply been pointing out that the rules do not require that Focus always be ignored when considering spheres - not that I\u2019ve found, anyway.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>this is literally how A bit of Spirit and Chi effects in HDYDT are written, that the fact that they are a shaman, and thus communicating with spirits for every effect means Spirit 2 or higher is required. And the fact they are using Chi and therefore manipulating quintessence with every effect means they requires Prime 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, first thing to note is that if you are trying to get support from the order of this procedure, obviously you don\u2019t know an <i>explicit</i> statement in the rules to back up the idea that Focus must be kept so distinct from the spheres given for an effect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>a step by step accord that has Spheres regarded as the foundation at step 1 seems pretty explicit to me. Start with the Spheres, then consider the focus. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Secondly, I don\u2019t know about you, but when stating my intent in any reasonably freeform system, I\u2019m often inclined to say things like \u201cI call upon the spirits to make the fire dance,\u201d or \u201cI draw chi from the life around me, and channel that energy into my friend to close the wound.\u201d If there\u2019s an observable change (and with Prime, movement of chi/Quintessence is observable) then I think that\u2019s part of the effect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If my players say \u201cI call upon the spirits to make the fire dance.\u201d I will ask them if they intend to pierce the gauntlet. If yes, then it requires Spirit, if no then it would just be a Forces effect.<br /> <br /> Same goes with the chi healing effect, I will ask them are they going to enchant their friend with quintessence (such as make them able to soak agg damage). If yes then Prime would be appropriate, of they instead say \u201cno, I just want to heal his damage\u201d I will say, ok, that\u2019s a Life effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And when I get to step 2, I could easily see myself saying, as a player, \u201cWell, no, I don\u2019t believe I can heal; not without manipulating chi/Quintessence, and that isn\u2019t happening here.\u201d And that sends me back to Step 1 to think through my casting again.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds more like you\u2019ve taken the Crucial Component flaw, and selected Quintessence as a subset of the Energy instrument. Any form of quintessence would be good for the 2pt variant. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So when doing these things just drop the Sphere.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am having trouble understanding what you mean here. If you can easily drop the need for an entire sphere, does that mean all effect that rely on that sphere become a permanent -1 diff?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I\u2019m not dictating anything. Players build their characters. They choose what limitations they build into them (negotiated with me to produce reasonable fairness across the group). I inform them of the consequences of their choices before they are committed to those choices.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>that is what the Crucial Component flaw is for though. If you want to make it an individual thing for each player, use the flaw rather than mix focus and spheres together, that sort of thing only leads to confusion otherwise. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why do you suppose players will build these characters?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an old joke\u2026 A man walks into his doctor\u2019s office, and says, \u201cDoc, it hurts when I do this.\u201d The doctor replies, \u201cDon\u2019t do that. Next!\u201d<br /> <br /> These types of objections are meaningless. You say problems occur if somebody does some particular, and particularly useless, thing. The solution is that we just don\u2019t do that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do all Shamans require the Spirit sphere? If the answer is no then that means this build of Shaman is possible. I personally don\u2019t think a shaman archetype has to be capable of piercing the gauntlet just to use their practice, and as such, a Forces or Life only shaman is fine. <br /> <br /> what your ruling does is make such a character non-viable. You make it so a player must take Spirit in order to be a shaman.<br /> <br /> If you have two players, both shaman, one does bot want to have Spirit and the other does but both have Forces, are you going to treat their uses of Forces magic differently?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly what difficulty break rule are you referring to here? There\u2019s a couple of different ways to reduce difficulty, and I do not know which you are referring to or how it applies.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Using tools you have sheded as a result of increased arete<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see no reason that the possibility of effect spheres being affected by the means used to cast the effect would require any of that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>if you require a mage who makes wind by communing with the spirits need Spirit, then it follows that you should also require a mage who uses their mental will to create wind requires Mind, one who uses their relationship with the gods of Fate to call a wind require Entropy, one who uses their mastery of elements via alchemy to conjure wind require Matter. Because in each instant, the way they are calling the Forces effect involves something which is arguably within the purview of another sphere, as is the case with the Bit of Spirit ruling.<br /> <br /> it would be logically inconsistent to not do the same with Matter for Alchemy, Mind for manifestation of Will, Entropy for manifestation via the gods of fate.<br /> <br /> heck, you could even argue any magic that involves herbs or plants as an instrument requires Life by the same token. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, in summary, there\u2019s certainly nothing explicitly stating your position in the rules, and so far I really wouldn\u2019t consider any of your attempts at deducing support from what is in the rules to be conclusive. (Noting that there is one where I\u2019m not sure which rule you are referring to.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>my aim here is to adequately explain my reasoning to you. If you want to throw it all away and say \u201cyeah, but I\u2019m still right\u201d you go ahead and do that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I told you it\u2019s not an issue. I just didn\u2019t assume that adding a new use for Quintessence also meant dropping the Feats of Focussed Chi in their regular context.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you mean by this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And all I said about that is that I don\u2019t see why we wouldn\u2019t just give -1 difficulty for the Quintessence expenditure if somebody was using that in the usual fashion.<br /> <br /> I never suggested doing that. Prime is required to channel Quintessence, not to spend personal Quintessence.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>these two statements contradict each other. If you say chi healing uses Prime 2 to let you spend quint to reduce difficulty, then you can\u2019t then say you never claimed prime 2 is required to reduce difficulty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not when you\u2019re talking about chiminage, we\u2019re not. I am familiar with that term (having played Werewolf: the Apocalypse a fair bit) but it\u2019s not in the M20 core book at all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Chiminage is mentioned by name in the Book of Secrets under the Fetish section<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520588#post1520588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And sure, the M20 rules are designed to be flexible, and allow you to introduce your vision of shamanism, but that also means there is scope and support for other approaches too.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>that is what the Crucial Component flaw is for\u2026<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T18:04:11-07:00","id":1520730,"title":"","content":"To be fair, there's a playstyle for Mage that disregards most or all of the Merits and Flaws; and technically, Merits and Flaws are supposed to be optional anyway. So \u201cthat's what Crucial Component is for\u201d is mildly problematic. <br /> <br /> But only <i>mildly</i> problematic, because you can always play <i>as if</i> you had a particular Flaw, even if you don't. So the text of Crucial Component can be read as a guideline for how to handle a mage who believes that a particular component is crucial. And frankly, that's <i>not </i>\u201cadd another Sphere to the requirements.\u201d <br /> <br /> Finally, I'm going to disagree with the assertion that you need to apply Prime 2 to an Effect if the mage has the Energy Instrument and chooses to define the Energy as Quintessence. We already have evidence that not everything that involves shifting Quintessence around requires Prime; see the aforementioned \u201cspend Quintessence to lower the Effect's difficulty\u201d for an example. If the \u201cshifting Quintessence around\u201d is purely for flavor, then I see no need to add Prime to the Effect's Sphere requirements. Ditto with A Bit of Spirit and the one about requiring Mind for effects because you're using the Psionics Practice: if it's just for flavor, there's no need to add Spirit or Mind to the prerequisites. <br /> <br /> And when HDYDT adds do-nothing Spheres to an Effect, you have three options: roll with it; discard the unnecessary Spheres; or find something for those Spheres to do. The first is what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11151\" data-vbnamecard=\"11151\">travisjhall</a> is doing, albeit in a rather aggressive way (sorry travis; but you're coming across as doing exactly what you've accused Saikou of doing: insisting on continuing to argue until the other party capitulates to your position); the third is the premise of this thread \u2014 which is why, if you don't disagree that it's a valid approach to use, you might want to just stop arguing. Nobody is trying to tell you not to do what you're doing, we're just explaining why the thread's premise is an acceptable alternative to that. <br /> <br /> (Note that I skipped the second option. That's because nobody is going around saying \u201cI don't understand why you don't just drop the useless Spheres\u201d, and then claiming that they're being told how to play the game when and explanation is given.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T01:14:33-07:00","id":1520750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520686#post1520686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Due to context: The difficulty break that happens when you surpass an Instrument, yet use it ayway. Since Spheres are immaterial, ever present parts of your Character Sheet, and there seems to be a consensus that adding the Sphere has no drawbacks, you could add it all the time.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's that big of a deal. It's an advantage of all Instruments that are &quot;part of the mage&quot;, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see a bit of leakage from the other thread I started here, and I\u2019ve been trying to avoid that. I\u2019d rather not have that conversation take over Saikou\u2019s thread and supplant discussion of his idea.<br /> <br /> But yes, if that\u2019s the rule we\u2019re talking about here\u2026 In M20 the ability to get a bonus from using an instrument you don\u2019t have to is completely independent from the spheres involved in the effect. The player just declares an intent to use their Energy instrument to cast a Forces effect, and they get the bonus. Adding in Prime gets no further reduction. You\u2019re right, Aleph, about this being no different to the regular application of this rule.<br /> <br /> Back in Revised, a mage had an instrument linked to each sphere. However, I checked the equivalent rule there. In that edition, you got the reduction to difficulty if the effect uses <i>only</i> the spheres for which you have surpassed the tool, and you use the tool for all of those spheres in the effect. So in that case, you still can\u2019t get a bonus from adding Prime to everything. If you have a Forces effect, and you\u2019ve surpassed your Forces tool, you can just use your Forces tool get the bonus. If you have surpassed your Prime tool, and add your Prime into the effect, that just means you have to use both tools to get the same bonus. And if you are doing a Matter effect (for example) and you haven\u2019t surpassed your Matter tool, you won\u2019t get a bonus for using surpassed tools regardless of what other spheres are added in.<br /> <br /> (I do not intend to go back to earlier editions to see what they did.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520686#post1520686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does &quot;we just don\u2019t do that&quot; mean?. The implication it's &quot;we don't play a Shaman without Spirit 2&quot;, but that's a case-by-case thing...while I've never played a Shaman w/o Spirit 2, I can imagine psionic-like characters w/o Mind 2 (not all psions are empath/telepath), and I actually favor Martial Artists that understood Chi as the flows of Life rather than the more &quot;energy-like&quot; dupla of Prime/Quintessence</div> </div> </div> </div>It means, don\u2019t build a character for use as a PC who is so restricted they won\u2019t be fun to play (which is the real problem here).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no conceptual problem with a character who is using a Focus that requires them to use Spirit 2 to do pretty much everything, and not enough Spirit expertise to satisfy that requirement. Even with higher other spheres. They pretty much suck as a mage\u2026 but as an NPC, that could be valid as an apprentice for whom magick just hasn\u2019t properly clicked yet. Maybe one day things will finally come together for them, represented by gaining the second dot of Spirit, and boom, suddenly they are throwing around fireballs with the Forces 3 they\u2019ve had sitting in the background for ages. NPCs are allowed to suck. It\u2019s just not often going to make for a good PC. So don\u2019t. Play something else.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also no problem with different types of Shamans existing in the same world, with somewhat different Shamanic Foci. So if you want to play a Shaman with Spirit 1 (or no Spirit at all) and a Focus that doesn\u2019t require higher Spirit to use other spheres, just do that.<br /> <br /> As for Chi as flow of Life, I\u2019d be really interested to see one of my players implement something like that. It means that their Chi is not Quintessence, and that\u2019s fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520686#post1520686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like the idea of combining the Spheres the way you propose to create particular effects. Like, using Mind 3/Forces 3, instead of Prime 2/Forces 3, to conjure a fire with the power of your emotions or similar (understanding that this will deplete the mage's psyche). But when one says, &quot;psychics use their mind as a Focus, so it HAS to have at least Mind 2&quot;, that's <i>stronger of a claim</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not a claim that I have made. I\u2019m perfectly happy with both types of psychics existing in the same world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520686#post1520686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could think that implies I would be using it even if I'm NOT actually creating fire with the power of my emotions/psyche, but rather have a more &quot;reality-warper&quot; like approach that uses psionics as explanation, and would be more comfortable by moving Quintessence arround.<br /> <br /> While <b><i>this may not be </i></b><i><b><i>what you mean</i></b>,</i> <b>but </b><i><b>the rule in HDYDT kinda does follow that path. </b></i>As per the rule: <i>assume that a mage whose reality-bending Arts involve her connection to the spiritual essence of the world needs a Spirit Sphere Rank of 2 or better (the Touch Spirit Effect), in addition\u200b...</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You can deduce various things from the observed fact that some mages are using a more restricted Focus than others. A mage who requires Mind 3 to create fire is probably doing something more fundamentally based on \u201cthe power of the mind\u201d (whatever you think that is) than one who is not. A mage who only uses effects produced via techniques only made possible using Spirit 2 can probably be accurately said to be more reliant on a spiritual connection than one who does not. If a player wants a mechanic to denote their character as the \u201cmost spiritual\u201d or similar, and doesn\u2019t want to tie their character so heavily to the Spirit sphere as to include it in every effect, it\u2019s up to them to find an alternative to express that, not another player to drop their use of A Little Bit of Spirit. Beyond that, there\u2019s nothing to decide which characters qualify for the rule other than the player, ST and/or group in general say so. Shamans will say that everyone is connected to the realm of the spirit. Are you connected enough to qualify? I don\u2019t know, you tell me.<br /> <br /> And then, Aleph, you get off into some pretty detailed criticism of A Little Bit of Spirit that I think is way off-topic in this thread. I\u2019d be happy to talk about that with you, but how about we take it to a new thread if we\u2019re going to do that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T03:15:14-07:00","id":1520756,"title":"","content":"This seems to be the crux of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520723#post1520723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have two players, both shaman, one does bot want to have Spirit and the other does but both have Forces, are you going to treat their uses of Forces magic differently?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve tried to be really explicit about this, but the message continues to not get through. I definitely would work out with each player separately how their magic works, and that definitely includes the possibility of one having Forces magic be contingent on Spirit, and another not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520723#post1520723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am having trouble understanding what you mean here. If you can easily drop the need for an entire sphere, does that mean all effect that rely on that sphere become a permanent -1 diff?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t think of any reason why it would mean that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520723#post1520723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using tools you have sheded as a result of increased arete</div> </div> </div> </div>Not tied to the spheres in use for an effect in M20, as far as I can see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520723#post1520723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my aim here is to adequately explain my reasoning to you. If you want to throw it all away and say \u201cyeah, but I\u2019m still right\u201d you go ahead and do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your reasoning. I can see how you can prefer to run MtA as you do. I don\u2019t find your reasoning to convince me that the game has to be run that way. That doesn\u2019t make me right, just leaves \u201ccorrectness\u201d ambiguous. And I\u2019m comfortable with a degree of ambiguity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T03:20:20-07:00","id":1520757,"title":"","content":"I am happy for you to remain unconvinced that which sphere an effect requires should not be influenced by the practice of a mage.<br /> <br /> Though I also believe I would not wish to play in such a game which made a sphere effects function as you describe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 08-16-2023, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T03:40:29-07:00","id":1520759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520730#post1520730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the \u201cshifting Quintessence around\u201d is purely for flavor,</div> </div> </div> </div>I hold the view that, in a roleplaying game, flavour always has the potentially to really matter. (To some extent, one could say that the flavour is all that really matters.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520730#post1520730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first is what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11151\" data-vbnamecard=\"11151\">travisjhall</a> is doing, albeit in a rather aggressive way (sorry travis; but you're coming across as doing exactly what you've accused Saikou of doing: insisting on continuing to argue until the other party capitulates to your position);</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I\u2019m stubborn rather than aggressive. The difference being that I really don\u2019t mind that others play the game the way they do, and don\u2019t want to convince anybody to change their approach, but yes, I do stand up an awfully long time in my attempts to have my position <i>acknowledged</i>. The amount of \u201cyou don\u2019t allow shamans without Spirit 2\u201d and similar is incredible.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I don\u2019t think everybody should be using HDYDT (since it obviously isn\u2019t what is wanted by a lot of people) but it would be nice for it to be \u201cthat book that is useful to others but not me\u201d rather than \u201cthat book that is against the rules of the game\u201d.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T03:58:59-07:00","id":1520760,"title":"","content":"So you don't mind if others don't agree with you; and others don't mind if you don't agree with them. Got it. So why are you still arguing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T05:04:29-07:00","id":1520762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520760#post1520760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you don't mind if others don't agree with you; and others don't mind if you don't agree with them. Got it. So why are you still arguing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I do mind when others fail to or even do not attempt to understand my position, and especially if they misrepresent my position. (That whole \u201cif you think X, you do Y\u201d thing. Look at how much of my posts has been, \u201cNo, I don\u2019t do that at all. Why would I?\u201d)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T05:22:59-07:00","id":1520763,"title":"","content":"No one's attempting to misrepresent your position. What you're saying is people talking about how they see things differently than you. <br /> <br /> The difficulty you're facing is that you're in a thread based on the premise of adding functionality to otherwise useless Spheres, and your keep saying \u201cbut those Spheres <i>aren't</i> useless; <i>I</i> find that including them is perfectly valid. Why don't you?\u201d And then when someone explains why they don't, you respond with some form of \u201cdon't tell me how to run my games!\u201d<br /> <br /> I know <i>exactly</i> where you're coming from. I just don't agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T18:22:52-07:00","id":1520793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520762#post1520762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I do mind when others fail to or even do not attempt to understand my position, and especially if they misrepresent my position. (That whole \u201cif you think X, you do Y\u201d thing. Look at how much of my posts has been, \u201cNo, I don\u2019t do that at all. Why would I?\u201d)</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be mixing the threads here (they discuss practically the same issue, so if I am, no big deal), but I remember you saying thay such change was required due to lack of raw coverage of foci like psionics and telekinesis.<br /> <br /> One thing is to say how you prefer the game. You made it clear now that you give your players freedom and don't enforce those ridiculous HDYDT rules. That is good. To be honest, I believe every player on your table that plays a psionic will: A) Not want to add Mind as an instrument or B) Add Mind as an instrument, entirely based on the fact of tjey getting Mind in the first place or not. I am certain that not a single player that did not get the spheres (Mind, Spirit or whatever) would chose to go that path.<br /> <br /> So, the rule kinda doesn't make much sense for a lot of people. But hey, since you're not screwing your players with unecessary limits, that's cool.<br /> <br /> But don't say that this is a necessary house rule, because the books already cover that foci.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T05:27:24-07:00","id":1520800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520793#post1520793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be mixing the threads here (they discuss practically the same issue, so if I am, no big deal), but I remember you saying thay such change was required due to lack of raw coverage of foci like psionics and telekinesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand by what I said. However, I didn\u2019t say the change was required. (Obviously not, since the game has been played without a change there.) I said I don\u2019t find what is in the rules currently to be adequate if these questions arise, and I still don\u2019t. And I\u2019m sure I\u2019m not the only one, as it\u2019s one of the debates that goes back decades, and we see options written into rule books now because the debate has gone back decades.<br /> <br /> A change is not required\u2026 for those who are happy with the state of the rules, or for those who aren\u2019t happy with it but who haven\u2019t run into the problem areas in their games, But that doesn\u2019t mean that a change wouldn\u2019t help some others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520793#post1520793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing is to say how you prefer the game. You made it clear now that you give your players freedom and don't enforce those ridiculous HDYDT rules. That is good. To be honest, I believe every player on your table that plays a psionic will: A) Not want to add Mind as an instrument or B) Add Mind as an instrument, entirely based on the fact of tjey getting Mind in the first place or not. I am certain that not a single player that did not get the spheres (Mind, Spirit or whatever) would chose to go that path.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s fine. I\u2019d definitely encourage them to avoid that third category, and the other options have consequences.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T05:34:10-07:00","id":1520875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520800#post1520800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stand by what I said. However, I didn\u2019t say the change was required. (Obviously not, since the game has been played without a change there.) I said I don\u2019t find what is in the rules currently to be adequate if these questions arise, and I still don\u2019t. And I\u2019m sure I\u2019m not the only one, as it\u2019s one of the debates that goes back decades, and we see options written into rule books now because the debate has gone back decades.<br /> <br /> A change is not required\u2026 for those who are happy with the state of the rules, or for those who aren\u2019t happy with it but who haven\u2019t run into the problem areas in their games, But that doesn\u2019t mean that a change wouldn\u2019t help some others.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what people are telling you here is that the current rules already cover that (although you might not like it) and that your house rule do not really help (might even make it worse).<br /> <br /> I believe we are now discussing opinions, and we will have to agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520800#post1520800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s fine. I\u2019d definitely encourage them to avoid that third category, and the other options have consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>By consequences you mean the default drawbacks that practically every instrument have and is particular to them or you mean another house rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T16:06:26-07:00","id":1520907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520875#post1520875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what people are telling you here is that the current rules already cover that (although you might not like it) and that your house rule do not really help (might even make it worse).<br /> <br /> I believe we are now discussing opinions, and we will have to agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> By consequences you mean the default drawbacks that practically every instrument have and is particular to them or you mean another house rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is already a thread devoted to those discussions. If you actually want to make a useful contribution on the subject, you should make it there. Let\u2019s leave this thread for it\u2019s own topic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T18:29:47-07:00","id":1520916,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not a big fan of the house rule originally presented here (not because of any particular mechanical weakness; I just don\u2019t think prepared effects really fits very well with the paradigm - seems more D&amp;D wizard than mystic martial artist to me). There\u2019s nothing actually wrong about it, though, as house ruies go.<br /> <br /> But if somebody is looking for something for Prime to add to some of these Feats of Focussed Chi, and doesn\u2019t like the original suggestion here, I just stumbled across a possibility while reading up on something unrelated. From a rote in the Akashic Brotherhood tradition book: \u201cBecause of the use of Prime, the mage need not concentrate on the effect once cast.\u201d<br /> <br /> Now, that was a completely different style of rote, involving a much more long-term effect on a target (who is not the caster). And it is Prime 3, not Prime 2. (From prior to M20, though, an effects can get shifted or dropped between editions.) This doesn\u2019t use Quintessence, either.<br /> <br /> But you could steal the idea. Allow Prime 2 plus Quintessence expenditure to extend duration of an effect without requiring concentration. Prime because it\u2019s temporarily modifying the martial artist\u2019s pattern to sustain a magical ability on its own. And it seems to me that this fits reasonably well with the type of character being emulated, because if you watch the \u201cflying\u201d scenes in Hero, Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon, and similar movies, the characters seem very focussed on their fight, and not at all distracted by the flight that seems very natural to them.<br /> <br /> (Some of the feats are not duration-based, so this wouldn\u2019t apply, but those tend to be strikes anyway, and on those Prime 2 + Quintessence allows for aggravated damage.)<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like this enough to want to do it, but it is an idea to consider for anyone who is still looking for a Prime 2 effect that they are happy with in this area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T03:00:00-07:00","id":1521020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1520916#post1520916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not a big fan of the house rule originally presented here (not because of any particular mechanical weakness; I just don\u2019t think prepared effects really fits very well with the paradigm - seems more D&amp;D wizard than mystic martial artist to me). There\u2019s nothing actually wrong about it, though, as house ruies go.<br /> <br /> But if somebody is looking for something for Prime to add to some of these Feats of Focussed Chi, and doesn\u2019t like the original suggestion here, I just stumbled across a possibility while reading up on something unrelated. From a rote in the Akashic Brotherhood tradition book: \u201cBecause of the use of Prime, the mage need not concentrate on the effect once cast.\u201d<br /> <br /> Now, that was a completely different style of rote, involving a much more long-term effect on a target (who is not the caster). And it is Prime 3, not Prime 2. (From prior to M20, though, an effects can get shifted or dropped between editions.) This doesn\u2019t use Quintessence, either.<br /> <br /> But you could steal the idea. Allow Prime 2 plus Quintessence expenditure to extend duration of an effect without requiring concentration. Prime because it\u2019s temporarily modifying the martial artist\u2019s pattern to sustain a magical ability on its own. And it seems to me that this fits reasonably well with the type of character being emulated, because if you watch the \u201cflying\u201d scenes in Hero, Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon, and similar movies, the characters seem very focussed on their fight, and not at all distracted by the flight that seems very natural to them.<br /> <br /> (Some of the feats are not duration-based, so this wouldn\u2019t apply, but those tend to be strikes anyway, and on those Prime 2 + Quintessence allows for aggravated damage.)<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like this enough to want to do it, but it is an idea to consider for anyone who is still looking for a Prime 2 effect that they are happy with in this area.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with implementing your suggestion is it can be argued this is already the case by default for spells in M20, as it literally says any effects who\u2019s duration is set and has yet to run out does not contribute to the multiple effects limit.<br /> <br /> with revised, all effects contributed to this limit, and as a result it actually meant something to allow a spell to be exempt from this. But without some other house rules in place just to make this rulling worth considering, I don\u2019t think it is a great solution.<br /> <br /> To defend my own suggestion, think of it more like DBZ style powering up. They spend some time centring themselves, and then for the duration of the scene, they have access to these feats of power which are trigger upon the expenditure of quintessence.<br /> <br /> vulgar use may even appear like that heavy glow and surge of wind that is typical for the show.<br /> <br /> more subtle uses are like when a martial artists stands still for a moment before they attack, centring themselves, preparing themselves.<br /> <br /> less like prepped and ready, and more like a transformation ability, not unlike transforming in to a dragon and using quint to breath fire<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T04:53:21-07:00","id":1521023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1521020#post1521020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with implementing your suggestion is it can be argued this is already the case by default for spells in M20, as it literally says any effects who\u2019s duration is set and has yet to run out does not contribute to the multiple effects limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know. But that\u2019s why I said it could extend duration. An effect (by default, in M20) still requires concentration once its duration has ended.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t run through the implementation details, of course. I leave that for somebody who actually wants to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T06:40:45-07:00","id":1521026,"title":"","content":"I <i>do </i>like the idea of Prime allowing you to <i>invest </i>Quintessence in an ongoing Effect: the invested Quintessence becomes unavailable for however long the Effect lasts, and you get it back when the Effect ends. On the other hand, you don't need to achieve successes dedicated to Duration: the duration of the Effect <i>is </i>\u201chowever long the Quintessence is invested\u201d. (I'd also say that the amount of Quintessence invested serves as a buttress against anything that might end the Effect, such as countermagick or Unbelief.)<br /> <br /> That said, I might require a bit more than Prime 2 for this (it's a rather powerful option); and it's only really useful for <i>ongoing </i>Effects, so it generally doesn't help with Chi Magic Effects which tend <i>not</i> to be ongoing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T07:00:56-07:00","id":1521027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1521026#post1521026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>do </i>like the idea of Prime allowing you to <i>invest </i>Quintessence in an ongoing Effect: the invested Quintessence becomes unavailable for however long the Effect lasts, and you get it back when the Effect ends. On the other hand, you don't need to achieve successes dedicated to Duration: the duration of the Effect <i>is </i>\u201chowever long the Quintessence is invested\u201d. (I'd also say that the amount of Quintessence invested serves as a buttress against anything that might end the Effect, such as countermagick or Unbelief.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That\u2019s actually a pretty interesting implementation. (And if you\u2019re going for the DBZ-like interpretation, kind of explains why these characters start glowing as they power up.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520086-i-figured-out-chi-magic?p=1521026#post1521026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I might require a bit more than Prime 2 for this (it's a rather powerful option); and it's only really useful for <i>ongoing </i>Effects, so it generally doesn't help with Chi Magic Effects which tend <i>not</i> to be ongoing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Feats of Focussed Chi effects which are not ongoing are mostly (all?) strikes or healing. On those, the spent Quintessence already has an effect - allowing the damage to be aggravated, or the healing to restore aggravated damage. (Although the healing could be done on somebody without aggravated damage.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T07:53:35-07:00","id":1521028,"title":"","content":"\u2026and I wouldn't require Prime 2 if the healing Effect is used to heal bashing or lethal damage; nor would I require a Quintessence expenditure. Likewise, I could see adding Prime 2 to the Spirit-Strike to inflict aggravated damage to incorporeal targets; but if all you want to do is to punch a ghost, you should only need Spirit 2; and if you want to inflict harm as if you were using the Life Sphere, you should only need either Spirit 3 or Entropy 3; no Prime. <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <br /> Another option to consider would be to allow someone with Prime to spend Quintessence on additional successes instead of reduced difficulty: you can purchase no more than one success this way, and you must first achieve one success on the dice. <br /> <br /> I could get behind the idea of Prime giving you new ways of using Quintessence (i.e., investing it into ongoing Effects, or buying a success with it). I think I'd make Quintessence Investment a Prime 3 Effect; it strikes me as being conceptually similar to the Wonder crafting that first becomes available at Prime 3. But I could see the enhanced success option working at Prime 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T20:50:46-07:00","id":1521417,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve avoided bringing it up before because it\u2019s pretty edge-case, but technically I think Prime and the Quintessence spend are having a mechanical effect in Spirit Strike.<br /> <br /> First there\u2019s the simple Spirit 2 + Prime 2 + 1 Quintessence case. As mentioned, this will inflict aggravated punch damage on a spirit (manifested or not). Sure, Spirit 2 should let you inflict bashing punch damage on a spirit by itself, but if you want to upgrade to aggravated, you need Prime 2 and 1 Quintessence. What I\u2019ve been unsure about is whether aggravated damage makes any difference to spirits, but having been checking up on this, I think it should (in M20 - I haven\u2019t going looking for the spirit combat rules in earlier editions, and I don\u2019t intend to). Once the damage is taken by the spirit, it just reduces the spirit\u2019s essence, and it doesn\u2019t matter whether that is bashing, lethal, or aggravated (although possibly you could house rule longer recovery times for lethal or aggravated damage even for spirits). But I can\u2019t see anything that says spirits soak lethal and aggravated damage. They soak using Willpower instead of Stamina, but I haven\u2019t found anything about them soaking damage with Willpower when Stamina could not normally be used to soak. So, my inclination would be to say that a spirit can soak bashing damage with Willpower and the Armor charm (if it has that charm), can soak lethal damage only with the Armor charm, and cannot soak aggravated damage at all. And that makes Spirit Strike\u2019s most basic form mechanically useful.<br /> <br /> Then, of course, you\u2019ve got the Spirit 3 + Prime 2 + 1 Quintessence version. This inflicts damage as if using Life 3 on a regular living creature, which means reading the successes through the Base Damage table. And Life 3 can already inflict aggravated damage. However, Life 3 aggravated damage is always a vulgar effect. Nothing says that Prime 2 + 1 Quintessence aggravated damage is vulgar. (Punching someone in the soul is a lot more subtle than body horror-style gaping wounds opening.) So this combination allows reading successes through the Base Damage table as aggravated damage to a spirit as a coincidental effect. And a coincidental effect means a lower difficulty, and less paradox - a fair trade for 1 Quintessence, I think.<br /> <br /> And finally there\u2019s the Entropy 3 + Prime 2 + 1 Quintessence version, but that works the same as the Spirit 3 version on ghosts.<br /> <br /> Now, it has occurred to me that by the time a mage is punching spirits and ghosts, the ST might want to rule that everything is pretty vulgar anyway. That\u2019s a fair ruling that negates much of the above logic. If that\u2019s your approach, Spirit strike becomes not mechanically useful again. But I figure the above could be worth considering.<br /> <br /> And I think that means that all three strikes in Feats of Focussed Chi have mechanical effects. Between that an Dataweaver\u2019s interesting mechanic, that\u2019s 7 out of 8 Feats of Focussed Chi having mechanical reasons to be built that way.<br /> <br /> And the eighth is Chi Healing, which works fine when healing aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> And admittedly that leaves a dodgy Prime 2 and spending 1 Quintessence to healing bashing and lethal damage, but it\u2019s pretty good coverage overall. I think there\u2019s value in partial solutions, for those who don\u2019t like any of the suggested complete solutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}